<i>Oh mighty warriors, who are swimming</i>
<i>across the raging dark sea</i>

22
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:20,333
<i>Flying high, with fire in their hearts</i>

23
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:23,417
<i>As war drums turn thunderous</i>
<i>The world trembles in fear</i>

24
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:26,042
<i>The hidden black panthers</i>
<i>will run for their lives</i>

25
00:03:26,125 --> 00:03:29,500
<i>Everyone will retreat when faced with them</i>

26
00:03:43,042 --> 00:03:44,500
-Boss, food?
-Food?

27
00:03:44,583 --> 00:03:48,167
You eat it! Idiots, eating all the time...

28
00:03:54,958 --> 00:03:57,292
Aren't they gonna bring it?
Are they cheating me?

29
00:03:57,375 --> 00:03:59,958
-What, sir?
-Nothing. I was telling you to eat!

30
00:04:01,167 --> 00:04:03,208
These guys are so stupid.

31
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:12,083
Please give me something.

32
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,583
No, no. Get going!

33
00:04:22,458 --> 00:04:25,125
Enough. Come on, hurry up! Come on!

34
00:04:26,458 --> 00:04:28,500
-Sir, what's this?
-Keep quiet!

35
00:04:33,875 --> 00:04:36,125
Sir, I've received the item.

36
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:40,792
Just get there in one hour.
I'll have set things up by then.

37
00:04:41,583 --> 00:04:43,833
Let's make the whole thing
a little dramatic, okay?

38
00:04:44,125 --> 00:04:47,958
<i>Oh, queen of my dreams</i>
<i>When will you come?</i>

39
00:04:48,292 --> 00:04:49,292
Sing, man!

40
00:04:49,417 --> 00:04:52,333
<i>Oh, queen of my dreams</i>
<i>When will you come?</i>

41
00:04:58,375 --> 00:04:59,958
Such shrewd minds!

42
00:05:00,375 --> 00:05:03,333
They have sent it in pieces
so that no one would recognize it.

43
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:11,292
This is a game with our lives at risk.
You remember everything I said, right?

44
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:13,750
Travel by taking many different trains.

45
00:05:14,042 --> 00:05:16,542
Tamil Nadu Border.
The station's name is Gomangalam.

46
00:05:17,083 --> 00:05:18,417
They, and only they, will be there.

47
00:05:18,583 --> 00:05:20,875
It's a completely deserted
station otherwise.

48
00:05:21,208 --> 00:05:22,833
How will he recognize us?

49
00:05:23,708 --> 00:05:26,375
Just go to the station with the box.
They'll come to you.

50
00:05:26,708 --> 00:05:28,833
If we go without the box, they won't come?

51
00:05:29,333 --> 00:05:31,417
No. They won't come
if they don't see the box.

52
00:05:32,458 --> 00:05:34,292
You poor idiots!

53
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:37,292
Just go down
to the station like I told you.

54
00:05:38,625 --> 00:05:41,542
And if they give you money,
you know where to go, right?

55
00:05:42,208 --> 00:05:45,417
Don't call me under any circumstance.
It's the cyber age.

56
00:05:45,667 --> 00:05:48,125
There's a chance the police
will be able to track me.

57
00:05:48,833 --> 00:05:50,083
Once everything is over,

58
00:05:50,292 --> 00:05:53,708
send a message to me on WhatsApp
in code, so no one else could understand.

59
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:57,542
I'll repeat the station's name
one last time: Gomangalam.

60
00:05:57,833 --> 00:05:59,375
-What's the name?
-Mukesh Kumar.

61
00:06:04,667 --> 00:06:08,750
You fool! I said the station's name.
Gomangalam!

62
00:06:10,583 --> 00:06:13,167
Then without further delay,
hit me over the head.

63
00:06:13,375 --> 00:06:15,250
Knock me out, then go, fast!
They'll be here soon.

64
00:06:19,875 --> 00:06:21,500
Shetty wouldn't be fooled at all.

65
00:06:21,833 --> 00:06:23,792
Hit me hard, man! Well done!

66
00:06:45,667 --> 00:06:48,000
Friends, none of you believed me

67
00:06:48,083 --> 00:06:51,917
when I said that the crisis that began
two days back would be temporary.

68
00:06:52,417 --> 00:06:55,125
When I said that it would be
a blessing for us, you all suspected me.

69
00:06:55,250 --> 00:06:57,708
Now look! We are going to be millionaires!

70
00:06:59,708 --> 00:07:00,792
No, no need.

71
00:07:02,875 --> 00:07:03,792
Open it!

72
00:07:20,458 --> 00:07:21,917
What happened, Prabhakaran?

73
00:07:28,333 --> 00:07:30,208
Nobody move! Come on!

74
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:32,667
Don't move! All of you, hands up!

75
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:41,500
Suresh told us everything.

76
00:07:47,542 --> 00:07:48,750
We know everything.

77
00:08:10,958 --> 00:08:13,542
No, sir. He sustained a hard blow
on his head, sir.

78
00:08:14,333 --> 00:08:17,208
If this stuff gets onto
the black market somehow,

79
00:08:17,375 --> 00:08:19,583
the whole country will be in crisis.
You know that, right?

80
00:08:22,125 --> 00:08:24,375
I didn't know that one among them
would betray the others.

81
00:08:24,458 --> 00:08:26,000
Have you found out where it went?

82
00:08:26,167 --> 00:08:27,667
<i>Sir, we cracked his phone.</i>

83
00:08:28,125 --> 00:08:30,292
<i>There aren't any suspicious calls</i>
<i>or messages.</i>

84
00:08:30,458 --> 00:08:34,167
After Suresh delivered the item,
Prabhakaran didn't call anyone.

85
00:08:34,333 --> 00:08:35,458
<i>And the people we arrested?</i>

86
00:08:35,542 --> 00:08:38,083
They don't know where it is, sir.

87
00:08:38,208 --> 00:08:40,583
We'll only be able to find it
if he regains consciousness.

88
00:08:44,625 --> 00:08:46,792
So go and search for it, man!

89
00:09:03,958 --> 00:09:08,333
<i>Namaste. Speaking far away from the city,</i>
<i>this is Arakkal Abu from the High-Range.</i>

90
00:09:08,667 --> 00:09:11,125
<i>Did you notice? There was</i>
<i>something fishy about the train</i>

91
00:09:11,208 --> 00:09:12,875
<i>when it set off from Mangalore.</i>

92
00:09:13,167 --> 00:09:15,333
<i>It's always like that,</i>
<i>not just with trains.</i>

93
00:09:15,542 --> 00:09:18,708
<i>Even if North Korea fired</i>
<i>an atomic bomb at America,</i>

94
00:09:18,875 --> 00:09:21,875
<i>it would probably end up detonating</i>
<i>on Shaji Pappan's chest.</i>

95
00:09:22,208 --> 00:09:25,292
<i>Let it come. Even after that mess</i>
<i>with the exotic herb,</i>

96
00:09:25,417 --> 00:09:28,250
<i>Pappan is still here</i>
<i>with his old back pain and other problems.</i>

97
00:09:28,542 --> 00:09:30,917
<i>Apart from a slight fluctuation</i>
<i>in his attitude towards women,</i>

98
00:09:31,167 --> 00:09:34,083
<i>Pappan is the same old Pappan.</i>
<i>Even with us.</i>

99
00:09:35,792 --> 00:09:36,792
Hey!

100
00:09:37,417 --> 00:09:40,917
We should get this cow dung to our village
before evening. It smells so bad!

101
00:09:41,292 --> 00:09:43,208
I'm driving a cow dung lorry
for the first time.

102
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,958
As if! You were driving
Ambani's car before this.

103
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:50,417
Faster, man! There's a cross
right in front of the lorry.

104
00:09:50,792 --> 00:09:51,792
Will we get in trouble?

105
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:53,542
Yes, here we go.

106
00:09:54,042 --> 00:09:56,167
-The bridge is full of those mad men.
-Sir, a lorry is coming.

107
00:09:58,375 --> 00:09:59,375
Stop!

108
00:10:00,417 --> 00:10:03,292
Looks like we're in trouble.
How do we get out of this mess?

109
00:10:04,083 --> 00:10:05,750
-Hold this.
-Get down fast!

110
00:10:09,208 --> 00:10:10,292
What's in the vehicle?

111
00:10:10,542 --> 00:10:12,792
It's manure for Shaji Pappan's
plantation, sir.

112
00:10:12,875 --> 00:10:14,042
Do you want some cow dung, sir?

113
00:10:14,125 --> 00:10:16,917
Who is this Shaji Pappan?
Is he an estate owner?

114
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
-Shaji Pappan?
-Give it here.

115
00:10:20,042 --> 00:10:21,708
-Did you come via Marayur?
-Yes.

116
00:10:21,792 --> 00:10:24,167
And there's no sandalwood
hidden in the manure?

117
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:26,542
-Sandalwood?
-Tell the truth, are you smugglers?

118
00:10:26,625 --> 00:10:29,833
Why are you trying to misrepresent
the case, sir, just like the media?

119
00:10:29,958 --> 00:10:31,458
Shut up, scum!

120
00:10:31,542 --> 00:10:33,375
I'll decide whether it's sandalwood
or just manure.

121
00:10:33,917 --> 00:10:36,750
PC, unload the whole thing.
And search under the platform.

122
00:10:37,167 --> 00:10:39,750
Sir, you can unload the manure
and search the platform,

123
00:10:40,333 --> 00:10:43,500
-but you'll need to load it all back up.
-And if we don't?

124
00:10:44,083 --> 00:10:45,583
If the manure doesn't reach
the plantation,

125
00:10:45,667 --> 00:10:49,833
-you'll have to answer to Pappan.
-Go and tell him about it!

126
00:10:50,417 --> 00:10:52,542
-Cleetus?
-I'll answer him myself!

127
00:10:52,625 --> 00:10:54,208
Now you throw the ball. I'll bat.

128
00:10:54,292 --> 00:10:55,750
-What?
-Call him!

129
00:10:55,833 --> 00:10:56,708
Keep quiet, umpire!

130
00:10:56,792 --> 00:10:58,917
I'll show you who's the umpire
when we get to the station!

131
00:11:01,875 --> 00:11:04,000
That won't be necessary now, sir.
They're here.

132
00:11:04,667 --> 00:11:05,792
Pappan!

133
00:11:26,417 --> 00:11:27,750
It's Abu?

134
00:11:28,375 --> 00:11:31,208
<i>Abu is a terror</i>
<i>An absolute devil</i>

135
00:11:31,292 --> 00:11:33,292
<i>The death-God's wingman</i>
<i>Lover of blood</i>

136
00:11:33,375 --> 00:11:35,583
<i>He combs his hair with a sword</i>

137
00:11:35,667 --> 00:11:38,708
<i>Chopping heads is his hobby</i>

138
00:11:40,542 --> 00:11:42,833
<i>Abu is a terror</i>
<i>An absolute devil...</i>

139
00:11:43,333 --> 00:11:44,875
Who is this?

140
00:11:45,292 --> 00:11:47,292
<i>He combs his hair with a sword</i>

141
00:11:47,792 --> 00:11:50,667
<i>Chopping heads is his hobby</i>

142
00:11:57,583 --> 00:11:59,083
Pappan isn't there?

143
00:12:00,875 --> 00:12:03,125
-Come!
-Leave me, sir.

144
00:12:07,958 --> 00:12:11,250
Is it really necessary to involve
Shaji Pappan in cases of cow dung, sir?

145
00:12:12,708 --> 00:12:14,208
-Am I not good enough?
-And who are you?

146
00:12:14,292 --> 00:12:15,875
It's good that you don't know.

147
00:12:16,708 --> 00:12:19,792
I am Abu. Arakkal Abu.

148
00:12:21,583 --> 00:12:22,583
Just ask them.

149
00:12:24,583 --> 00:12:27,250
You don't have to ask us.
He's Arakkal Abu.

150
00:12:27,875 --> 00:12:31,958
So, just leave Shaji Pappan's boys
and his lorry alone.

151
00:12:32,792 --> 00:12:34,833
Are you telling the police
how to do justice, you rascal?

152
00:12:35,708 --> 00:12:37,583
Don't do that, sir. You'll be condemned.

153
00:12:38,083 --> 00:12:39,417
How dare you grab my hand?

154
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:41,917
<i>Shajiyetta!</i>

155
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,333
SHAJI PAPPAN

156
00:12:51,167 --> 00:12:53,042
Sir! No!

157
00:13:01,125 --> 00:13:03,250
<i>Shajiyetta!</i>

158
00:13:15,458 --> 00:13:19,167
<i>Even Haji Mastan would salute</i>
<i>the brave and mighty Shaji Pappan</i>

159
00:13:19,292 --> 00:13:22,917
<i>Even an atom bomb would defuse</i>
<i>on its own at the sight of Shaji Pappan</i>

160
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:26,500
<i>Even Haji Mastan would salute</i>
<i>the brave and mighty Shaji Pappan</i>

161
00:13:26,708 --> 00:13:28,833
<i>Even an atom bomb would defuse</i>
<i>on its own at the sight...</i>

162
00:13:28,958 --> 00:13:30,750
Is Pappan coming from Sabarimala?

163
00:13:30,833 --> 00:13:37,333
<i>Pappan is our darling</i>
<i>Pappan is our wealth</i>

164
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,375
-Oops.
-These are my boys, sir.

165
00:13:48,542 --> 00:13:49,750
This is just manure, right?

166
00:13:50,792 --> 00:13:53,000
-Leave it alone.
-Who are you to tell me that?

167
00:14:19,292 --> 00:14:20,875
If anyone touches Pappan...

168
00:14:22,208 --> 00:14:25,458
-then Pappan will decide their destiny!
-Kill him, Pappan!

169
00:14:27,875 --> 00:14:29,625
Pappan, I just said that
out of excitement!

170
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:38,750
Run for your lives! Or Pappan will throw
all of you to the water.

171
00:14:38,875 --> 00:14:40,292
-Really?
-I swear!

172
00:14:40,417 --> 00:14:41,917
Then let's scram!

173
00:14:42,958 --> 00:14:45,125
-Sir, you know how to swim, right?
-Hey!

174
00:14:46,042 --> 00:14:50,250
What did you think?
That Pappan was a third-rate smuggler?

175
00:14:51,167 --> 00:14:56,458
My forefathers conquered mountains, fought
wars with wild animals and plundered gold!

176
00:14:57,083 --> 00:14:58,083
When did that happen?

177
00:14:58,250 --> 00:15:00,500
-It happened.
-Really? Then continue.

178
00:15:00,833 --> 00:15:02,917
So, me and my boys,
who have such a history,

179
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,125
needn't make a living
by smuggling sandalwood!

180
00:15:05,542 --> 00:15:09,500
Swim! Not even the alligators
want your stinking blood!

181
00:15:09,958 --> 00:15:12,125
We'll wait at the station! You hear me?

182
00:15:12,583 --> 00:15:13,583
That's right.

183
00:15:13,958 --> 00:15:15,875
I just remembered.
There's a small problem.

184
00:15:16,083 --> 00:15:17,000
What? Give me some water.

185
00:15:17,125 --> 00:15:19,917
Shajiyetta, we're in dire need
of money now, right?

186
00:15:20,083 --> 00:15:20,958
When are we not?

187
00:15:21,042 --> 00:15:22,833
Tug of war matches are not happening,
right?

188
00:15:22,958 --> 00:15:25,083
When Abukka told us, we
also thought it's right.

189
00:15:26,375 --> 00:15:29,792
In the lorry, below the cow dung,
there is a little sandalwood.

190
00:15:31,625 --> 00:15:32,667
Very little.

191
00:15:34,458 --> 00:15:35,375
Sandalwood?

192
00:15:35,542 --> 00:15:37,958
We kept it to get rid
of the cow dung stink.

193
00:15:38,042 --> 00:15:39,042
Sir!

194
00:15:39,542 --> 00:15:43,417
-Do you need a rope or something?
-Get lost! I'll get you later.

195
00:15:45,292 --> 00:15:49,625
God... What atrocity have you done,
Cleetus?

196
00:15:49,833 --> 00:15:51,167
<i>For trying to smuggle sandalwood,</i>

197
00:15:51,250 --> 00:15:54,042
<i>and trying to kill the duty officer</i>
<i>SI Pradeep Kumar who stopped them,</i>

198
00:15:54,208 --> 00:15:57,833
<i>by throwing him to the dam</i>
<i>from the Kambanamedu bridge,</i>

199
00:15:57,958 --> 00:15:59,917
<i>Pannimattathil Shaji Pappan</i>
<i>is accused in these cases.</i>

200
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:02,750
<i>Bail is allowed for the accused</i>
<i>with the guarantee of 50,000 rupees</i>

201
00:16:02,875 --> 00:16:04,375
<i>and two persons.</i>

202
00:16:04,625 --> 00:16:07,958
<i>And the court orders him to go and sign in</i>
<i>at the local police station every Monday,</i>

203
00:16:08,083 --> 00:16:12,417
<i>and not to leave the district</i>
<i>without the permission of the court</i>

204
00:16:12,625 --> 00:16:14,250
<i>until the trial is completed.</i>

205
00:16:14,458 --> 00:16:16,458
<i>The date of the trial</i>
<i>will be announced soon.</i>

206
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,625
Oh, my God! Terrorist!

207
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,708
-Don't run, Aashaan!
-I won't run!

208
00:17:09,667 --> 00:17:13,750
So it was you? I had told them
never to permit you inside.

209
00:17:14,125 --> 00:17:17,125
They didn't let me in.
So I jumped the wall and came in.

210
00:17:17,542 --> 00:17:21,417
-Please help me!
-Sir, I'm feeling cold.

211
00:17:22,250 --> 00:17:24,792
-Get out! Bloody gunman!
-Yes sir.

212
00:17:25,292 --> 00:17:30,042
<i>A thousand people will rise</i>
<i>From every drop of blood</i>

213
00:17:33,667 --> 00:17:37,292
Don't make me talk about what happened in
the name of the protest behind the bush!

214
00:17:38,125 --> 00:17:40,042
Who got irritated when I said that?

215
00:17:41,458 --> 00:17:44,875
That's the traditional style
of this PP Shashi.

216
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,125
Let them come.

217
00:17:48,292 --> 00:17:50,917
Even if all the media comes,
I will say, "Get out"

218
00:17:51,083 --> 00:17:54,500
and stand strong like a baton tank.
That's this PP Shashi.

219
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,792
That's our party's new slogan. Tell them!

220
00:18:00,958 --> 00:18:01,958
Sir...

221
00:18:02,792 --> 00:18:04,625
-My cap!
-Your trap!

222
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:07,708
When I became a minister, the first thing
I enquired for was your cap.

223
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:10,500
That has been on my table
as a paperweight for a long time

224
00:18:10,583 --> 00:18:12,625
and it will remain there
for even more time.

225
00:18:14,042 --> 00:18:18,333
What's that sacred mark on your forehead?
It looks like the party symbol!

226
00:18:25,792 --> 00:18:26,708
Drink it!

227
00:18:26,792 --> 00:18:29,333
The party workers and villagers
squeezed the juice out of me.

228
00:18:30,667 --> 00:18:33,083
-It was me who sent them.
-I was sure about that.

229
00:18:33,792 --> 00:18:35,083
This is the 17th time,

230
00:18:35,167 --> 00:18:37,625
that I've been trying to meet you
at the minister's office and your house.

231
00:18:38,375 --> 00:18:40,333
I can't live without my cap!

232
00:18:40,417 --> 00:18:44,583
-No?
-Revolutionary Lion! Please help me!

233
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:47,125
Help me!

234
00:18:53,375 --> 00:18:55,792
My enemies are on the rise
at the High Range.

235
00:18:56,750 --> 00:19:00,375
The other day someone threw
the Anangappara SI into the dam.

236
00:19:01,042 --> 00:19:05,875
Apart from me throwing something
to feed the fish in the dam,

237
00:19:06,542 --> 00:19:09,667
I don't like anyone else throwing
even a stone into the dam!

238
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:11,958
So...

239
00:19:13,208 --> 00:19:17,375
-I need a slave there!
-Aashaan!

240
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:22,583
Aashaan! I am that slave, Aashaan!

241
00:19:22,958 --> 00:19:25,708
I will take very good care of you
and your boys!

242
00:19:25,792 --> 00:19:28,208
Don't ditch me, sir! Please!

243
00:19:28,875 --> 00:19:30,833
<i>When I asked him decently,</i>
<i>he was arrogant.</i>

244
00:19:31,167 --> 00:19:32,583
<i>The arrogance that he became a minister.</i>

245
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,625
Finally, I locked the door of that room.

246
00:19:36,583 --> 00:19:39,125
Without understanding anything,
he sat there like a scared kitten,

247
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:41,625
our Home Minister. PP Shashi.

248
00:19:42,458 --> 00:19:44,625
I kept the gun I had with me on his table.

249
00:19:45,458 --> 00:19:46,625
Then just one dialogue!

250
00:19:46,708 --> 00:19:48,958
But wasn't your gun seized
while you were suspended?

251
00:19:49,083 --> 00:19:50,792
-Yes.
-Then which gun is this?

252
00:19:51,458 --> 00:19:54,000
A new gun which I got to kill your dad!
Listen to the story, rascal!

253
00:19:54,292 --> 00:19:56,833
-Sir.
-PC, just tell him about me.

254
00:19:57,125 --> 00:20:00,958
I told him, sir. He might have forgotten.
What is this?

255
00:20:01,958 --> 00:20:04,458
-So where did we stop?
-Fire! No. Gun!

256
00:20:04,583 --> 00:20:07,583
Yes. The gun! Then I said,

257
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:09,250
"You can make one choice.

258
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,125
Either I will leave the room with my cap,

259
00:20:12,958 --> 00:20:15,875
or my bullet will pierce your chest!

260
00:20:17,042 --> 00:20:19,792
You can decide what you want
among these two."

261
00:20:20,667 --> 00:20:24,542
Everyone got scared...
Silence all around...

262
00:20:25,375 --> 00:20:26,917
an eerie silence.

263
00:20:28,167 --> 00:20:31,333
-Sir!
-God! The party men!

264
00:20:37,625 --> 00:20:40,333
-Him?
-God! This trouble-maker?

265
00:20:40,875 --> 00:20:41,958
What?

266
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:46,792
What's up, sir? You've become dark.

267
00:20:47,375 --> 00:20:50,542
You've come here this morning to sign in,
have you joined the police?

268
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:56,833
Not that, sir.
The ex-SI Pradeep Kumar sir,

269
00:20:57,208 --> 00:20:59,208
I threw him into the dam.

270
00:20:59,292 --> 00:21:00,167
Oh my, it fell down.

271
00:21:00,333 --> 00:21:02,625
That's how this case happened.
They asked me to come and sign.

272
00:21:02,750 --> 00:21:04,417
Shall I make him sign, sir?

273
00:21:04,583 --> 00:21:05,917
-Let's sign?
-Yeah.

274
00:21:12,333 --> 00:21:13,500
What's that? A mountain?

275
00:21:13,583 --> 00:21:15,250
-No. It's a shoe.
-Shoe, it seems.

276
00:21:15,375 --> 00:21:17,208
Still going on with tug of war
and messing around?

277
00:21:17,292 --> 00:21:19,000
Tug of war is like oxygen for us, sir.

278
00:21:19,125 --> 00:21:20,042
No messing around.

279
00:21:20,125 --> 00:21:23,125
Actually, I didn't do anything to him.
He tripped and fell into the water.

280
00:21:23,458 --> 00:21:24,708
If that is so, then good for you!

281
00:21:24,833 --> 00:21:26,583
If not, I'll remove your spine
and make a stick.

282
00:21:26,667 --> 00:21:27,625
I know that, sir.

283
00:21:27,708 --> 00:21:30,333
Come here and sign every week
and you cannot leave the district!

284
00:21:30,583 --> 00:21:32,375
Then I'll sign in
for the whole six months, now.

285
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,375
-Isn't that a good idea, sir?
-No.

286
00:21:34,542 --> 00:21:37,042
-You can't do that, Pappan.
-I can't?

287
00:21:37,708 --> 00:21:38,792
-Okay, then.
-Get going!

288
00:21:40,208 --> 00:21:41,792
What's this? A hippo?

289
00:21:42,958 --> 00:21:43,875
Yes?

290
00:21:43,958 --> 00:21:45,625
He's showing disrespect towards me.

291
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,875
We should lock him up as soon as possible
and teach him to respect me.

292
00:21:55,667 --> 00:21:58,792
Why is she shouting like this?

293
00:21:59,083 --> 00:22:00,875
-Stop shouting!
-Shaji Pappan!

294
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,583
-Not smuggling sandalwood today?
-Why do you need sandalwood?

295
00:22:03,708 --> 00:22:07,292
To cremate your father? Bloody scum-bag!

296
00:22:11,792 --> 00:22:14,625
You? I thought it was my mom! What is it?

297
00:22:14,958 --> 00:22:17,625
Go mend that jackfruit tree.
You just sit here ogling all the time!

298
00:22:17,708 --> 00:22:18,750
Get up and come!

299
00:22:19,875 --> 00:22:22,375
Poor thing. I should have killed it
and eaten it back when I had the chance.

300
00:22:25,250 --> 00:22:28,792
<i>An adorable goat</i>

301
00:22:28,917 --> 00:22:32,417
<i>A sweet goat</i>

302
00:22:36,125 --> 00:22:39,875
Pinky! Your kids are so greedy!
Shall I have them butchered?

303
00:22:40,042 --> 00:22:42,000
These are the only earning members
of this house.

304
00:22:42,333 --> 00:22:43,958
-And you want to kill them?
-That's true.

305
00:22:44,167 --> 00:22:47,917
Hey! Where's the money that you got
by selling milk and that little goat?

306
00:22:48,417 --> 00:22:50,667
I won't give you a single penny from that.

307
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,833
I've put it in a piggy bank
to buy a Honda Activa.

308
00:22:52,917 --> 00:22:54,417
I don't need it, anyway.

309
00:22:54,542 --> 00:22:57,833
-You made such offers back then!
-I'll give it! Stop shouting.

310
00:22:58,292 --> 00:23:01,542
"Rachel dear, your father,
who is my brother, Thomas Pappan,

311
00:23:01,667 --> 00:23:04,542
just because he left you and mom,
don't worry.

312
00:23:04,667 --> 00:23:06,250
This Shaji Pappan
is there for you, right?"

313
00:23:06,375 --> 00:23:08,833
Even when my mom left, you said
that you'd be there for me!

314
00:23:09,167 --> 00:23:11,833
After making all these claims,
have you bought even a c<i>huridar </i>for me?

315
00:23:11,917 --> 00:23:14,000
-I need money for that, right?
-Money!

316
00:23:14,125 --> 00:23:16,542
Now you need me to take care
of your mom, these goats,

317
00:23:16,708 --> 00:23:18,000
and to apply hot bags on your back.

318
00:23:18,208 --> 00:23:20,333
You're so useless to everyone around you,
Pappan!

319
00:23:20,417 --> 00:23:22,583
I'll slice you! Wait and watch!

320
00:23:22,708 --> 00:23:24,958
To kill your sarcasm, I'll snatch
a huge deal soon enough!

321
00:23:25,083 --> 00:23:26,667
You're mocking me too much. I'll show you!

322
00:23:26,750 --> 00:23:28,125
-Irritating!
-I've heard this too many times.

323
00:23:28,208 --> 00:23:30,500
-Pappan!
-What?

324
00:23:30,958 --> 00:23:32,917
-There's a great deal!
-Deal?

325
00:23:33,417 --> 00:23:35,708
God is great! He brought a deal
right when I said it.

326
00:23:35,833 --> 00:23:38,542
-What deal is it, my boy?
-Come! Come!

327
00:23:39,333 --> 00:23:41,958
Get down guys...

328
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,917
Even the ex-Minister can read it
better than this.

329
00:23:46,042 --> 00:23:47,125
-Who's that?
-Give it here.

330
00:23:48,583 --> 00:23:50,333
-"Friend...
-It's from the Centre.

331
00:23:50,458 --> 00:23:52,958
...Pannimattath Varkey Pappan's son
Shaji Pappan."

332
00:23:53,042 --> 00:23:54,708
Is this the Bible? Read properly!

333
00:23:55,417 --> 00:23:58,000
"Since it is the Panchayat that has given
the property for the club,

334
00:23:58,083 --> 00:24:00,292
if 'Winner's Club' becomes inactive
anytime,

335
00:24:00,458 --> 00:24:02,625
or if the building is not refurbished,

336
00:24:02,833 --> 00:24:07,375
the Panchayat has the rights to seize
the building back and demolish it.

337
00:24:07,792 --> 00:24:10,042
And since the current condition
of the club is pathetic,

338
00:24:10,167 --> 00:24:14,750
the maximum time for refurbishing
and renovating the club will be one month.

339
00:24:14,875 --> 00:24:17,042
This is the Panchayat Ruling Committee's
decision.

340
00:24:17,250 --> 00:24:20,375
If the renovation work is not completed
within one month,

341
00:24:20,708 --> 00:24:23,750
the Panchayat will seize back the property
that was given to start the club.

342
00:24:24,042 --> 00:24:26,250
From President Uthup. Kappakkala."

343
00:24:27,042 --> 00:24:29,667
-Is this the bumper you brought?
-This is a seizure!

344
00:24:30,250 --> 00:24:33,000
Seizure? Then there will be drum rolls
and all, right?

345
00:24:33,167 --> 00:24:35,042
What do I do now, Jesus?

346
00:24:35,375 --> 00:24:37,958
Shajiyetta, he came and checked
out the club in the morning.

347
00:24:38,083 --> 00:24:40,333
Is this why he asked to give it
directly to Pappan without opening?

348
00:24:40,583 --> 00:24:43,042
-Mom, tea!
-Don't call her. That hag will come here!

349
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:45,708
Tea? Go ask your mom to make it.

350
00:24:46,083 --> 00:24:48,792
All the useless fellows have gathered
early in the morning?

351
00:24:48,917 --> 00:24:49,833
What is it?

352
00:24:50,125 --> 00:24:52,333
I heard you shouting
that there's some big bumper!

353
00:24:53,583 --> 00:24:54,458
Well,

354
00:24:54,542 --> 00:24:57,875
the Panchayat is going to give us an award
after seeing the functioning of our club.

355
00:25:00,708 --> 00:25:02,000
PRESIDENT
ANGANGAPARA VILLAGE PANCHAYAT

356
00:25:15,833 --> 00:25:18,042
Wear a little extra. Let the lips be rosy.

357
00:25:22,750 --> 00:25:24,083
Little devil!

358
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:29,750
It's blasphemy anyway.

359
00:25:30,542 --> 00:25:32,542
After your parents left you
at the convent,

360
00:25:32,750 --> 00:25:35,750
you started a fight there and hit
a nun on her chin,

361
00:25:35,917 --> 00:25:39,083
and came back home.
And because of that,

362
00:25:39,208 --> 00:25:42,083
I won't allow any alliance for her,
not just from this village,

363
00:25:42,542 --> 00:25:43,750
but any other village too.

364
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:46,167
I mean, I don't think anyone
would come running, anyway.

365
00:25:46,542 --> 00:25:48,042
-Right, Antony?
-Of course!

366
00:25:48,958 --> 00:25:52,458
I'm going to be very upfront
with everything about myself.

367
00:25:52,792 --> 00:25:55,958
I got both my daughters
married off to good families.

368
00:25:56,417 --> 00:26:00,375
Moreover, I have around 60 acres
and many shops in my name.

369
00:26:00,792 --> 00:26:03,417
And I have a great hold in politics.
Right, Antony?

370
00:26:04,083 --> 00:26:05,292
No liabilities at all!

371
00:26:06,833 --> 00:26:08,000
Then, shall I ask you something?

372
00:26:09,167 --> 00:26:11,333
Can you get her married to me?

373
00:26:13,333 --> 00:26:15,250
It's good that you get them married!

374
00:26:15,583 --> 00:26:17,958
Especially since Marcose Chettan
isn't well now.

375
00:26:18,167 --> 00:26:20,833
After the marriage, I will be there
for everything, right?

376
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:23,542
What's there to think about, sister?

377
00:26:23,625 --> 00:26:27,875
It's the neighbors who have a complained
because Uthup is unmarried.

378
00:26:28,167 --> 00:26:29,750
Especially women!

379
00:26:30,917 --> 00:26:32,042
It's out of love!

380
00:26:32,667 --> 00:26:34,750
-You didn't have tea.
-No. I have diabetes.

381
00:26:35,042 --> 00:26:37,167
-Then some mixture?
-No way! Blood pressure!

382
00:26:37,292 --> 00:26:41,375
What more do you need? Get them married!

383
00:26:41,583 --> 00:26:44,000
Let the children live happily! Right dear?

384
00:26:48,417 --> 00:26:51,792
-Everyone would be eating inside, right?
-All you can think about is food, right?

385
00:26:52,458 --> 00:26:53,458
Here they come!

386
00:26:53,750 --> 00:26:56,292
-He's wearing a wig, Shajiyetta!
-Hold me!

387
00:26:56,417 --> 00:26:59,583
-Don't you know that I have Arthritis?
-Looks like he is on old age pension.

388
00:27:01,417 --> 00:27:03,875
-Get down carefully.
-Looks like he's very healthy!

389
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:05,958
Yeah, right. I've heard that he studied
with Gandhiji.

390
00:27:06,083 --> 00:27:09,000
Aunty, Namaste. I haven't forgotten
about the toilet.

391
00:27:09,250 --> 00:27:11,958
All the losers are here? What's up, Shaji?

392
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:15,417
-I wanted to meet you.
-What's the matter?

393
00:27:15,708 --> 00:27:18,708
Nothing. About the club...

394
00:27:19,667 --> 00:27:22,667
Forget about it.
That's not going to happen!

395
00:27:22,792 --> 00:27:26,542
And, you should talk to that girl
and make her agree.

396
00:27:26,875 --> 00:27:28,208
You're neighbors, right?

397
00:27:28,375 --> 00:27:30,667
After the marriage,
we will be neighbors too, right?

398
00:27:30,917 --> 00:27:32,375
We should have a blast!

399
00:27:32,458 --> 00:27:35,458
If that happens, I will sort out
all the issues of your club.

400
00:27:35,875 --> 00:27:36,875
Start the car!

401
00:27:38,583 --> 00:27:41,083
If that's so, then why don't you get
that done, Pappan?

402
00:27:43,167 --> 00:27:45,375
Let's get Stella Chechi married to Pappan.

403
00:27:45,542 --> 00:27:48,125
The wounds from his first marriage
are still fresh.

404
00:27:48,417 --> 00:27:52,625
Anyway, marriage and family life
are not meant for such jobless people!

405
00:27:56,250 --> 00:27:59,500
Shajiyetta! Pappan, don't be sad!

406
00:27:59,667 --> 00:28:01,375
Just like Mohanlal walks away in <i>Kireedam</i>.

407
00:28:01,500 --> 00:28:02,833
Pappan became really sad.

408
00:28:11,750 --> 00:28:15,208
<i>We were all sad that we would also have</i>
<i>to sing sad songs with Shajiyettan,</i>

409
00:28:15,333 --> 00:28:17,500
<i>and live in grief hereafter.</i>

410
00:28:17,958 --> 00:28:20,042
<i>That's when it came on a cycle.</i>

411
00:28:26,917 --> 00:28:27,917
Catch!

412
00:28:28,792 --> 00:28:32,083
-Wow! Exactly like Mammootty!
-What is this?

413
00:28:32,583 --> 00:28:35,167
What's that?
Is it a notice for the next seizure?

414
00:28:35,375 --> 00:28:37,458
-What more can they seize from here?
-Let me read it.

415
00:28:42,458 --> 00:28:46,333
-Mahindra Baahubali!
-Mahendra Baahubali? Give it here!

416
00:28:46,542 --> 00:28:47,917
You don't know how to read.

417
00:28:49,542 --> 00:28:51,083
-It's in English!
-Give it back!

418
00:28:54,958 --> 00:28:56,250
Will Pappan get it?

419
00:28:56,583 --> 00:28:59,458
It's an international tournament.
Covers all of India.

420
00:28:59,792 --> 00:29:03,167
They have invited only our team
through a special letter.

421
00:29:03,708 --> 00:29:06,125
The registration fee itself
is 50,000 rupees.

422
00:29:06,500 --> 00:29:10,125
Then training, food, costumes,
all that would cost quite an amount.

423
00:29:10,708 --> 00:29:13,833
But if we win, we will get a cup
made with half a kilo of gold.

424
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:17,292
Cup made of half a kilo of gold?
So how many sovereigns would it be?

425
00:29:18,083 --> 00:29:19,417
Should be around 50.

426
00:29:20,583 --> 00:29:22,750
-That's great.
-Of course!

427
00:29:22,958 --> 00:29:25,708
If all of us pull strongly,
the cup will be in our hands.

428
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:28,417
Then who will you be? A princess!

429
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:30,083
-Smile!
-Get lost!

430
00:29:31,833 --> 00:29:34,542
But you should help us by giving us
a lot of money!

431
00:29:34,667 --> 00:29:36,000
What?

432
00:29:37,125 --> 00:29:39,375
By God's grace, I don't have
any money, right?

433
00:29:39,500 --> 00:29:41,292
So you should help me
for one last time, Mom!

434
00:29:41,375 --> 00:29:42,375
How?

435
00:29:44,292 --> 00:29:48,167
Our house's documents, can be mortgaged.
How does that sound?

436
00:29:49,583 --> 00:29:52,458
<i>You want my house's documents</i>
<i>for your useless club</i>?

437
00:29:52,583 --> 00:29:55,125
-What is this? Shadow play?
-Run! Run!

438
00:29:55,250 --> 00:29:57,917
-Get that shorty too!
-Is this a modern play?

439
00:29:58,042 --> 00:29:59,917
Don't hit me there. I have to get married.

440
00:30:00,083 --> 00:30:01,042
-Run!
-I will kill you today!

441
00:30:05,292 --> 00:30:07,750
Even though Mom objected,
I finally managed it.

442
00:30:08,042 --> 00:30:09,125
Did she give it?

443
00:30:09,583 --> 00:30:12,958
What Mom gave is seen on this forehead.
She didn't give it, man!

444
00:30:13,167 --> 00:30:15,042
I very smoothly stole the documents.

445
00:30:15,292 --> 00:30:17,250
I left a colored photocopy
in their place.

446
00:30:17,375 --> 00:30:21,458
-That was a great idea, Shajiyetta.
-Dude, there's only half an acre of land.

447
00:30:21,625 --> 00:30:23,250
If we lose that, we'll lose everything.

448
00:30:23,375 --> 00:30:25,625
We will win, Shajiyetta!
We will get the club back as well!

449
00:30:34,542 --> 00:30:37,542
God, protect this poor smuggler!

450
00:30:39,583 --> 00:30:40,583
God!

451
00:30:41,875 --> 00:30:44,667
Ikka, five or six people have come
to meet you today as well.

452
00:30:44,958 --> 00:30:46,333
God!

453
00:30:51,958 --> 00:30:54,167
The document is fine. It's original.

454
00:30:54,458 --> 00:30:56,708
I will give you 200,000 rupees.

455
00:30:56,833 --> 00:30:58,500
-And one more thing.
-What?

456
00:30:59,500 --> 00:31:02,042
-My interest rate is slightly high.
-Of course.

457
00:31:02,333 --> 00:31:06,250
When the time period is over,
you should bring me 230,000 rupees.

458
00:31:06,458 --> 00:31:09,417
Or else, one of my wives
will go to your house.

459
00:31:09,542 --> 00:31:12,292
What's wrong with that? No problem!
But there aren't many facilities.

460
00:31:12,583 --> 00:31:13,833
-Just tell her.
-Sure.

461
00:31:13,958 --> 00:31:17,125
After that, me and Ponnappan will reach
there with two beds and pillows.

462
00:31:18,250 --> 00:31:19,542
-What do you say?
-No!

463
00:31:19,667 --> 00:31:21,458
So, mercy and extra time,

464
00:31:21,625 --> 00:31:23,792
don't expect these two things
from Abdullah.

465
00:31:23,875 --> 00:31:26,583
I don't expect it. That's why I came here.

466
00:31:26,750 --> 00:31:30,042
Pappan, don't care about the documents.
Tug of war is more important for us.

467
00:31:30,458 --> 00:31:33,125
-You bloody--
-Then accept the money auspiciously.

468
00:31:33,250 --> 00:31:34,667
-Give it.
-You shouldn't take it.

469
00:31:38,125 --> 00:31:40,292
God! Please help me pay this back on time!

470
00:31:40,417 --> 00:31:43,250
-I hope he's never able to pay it back!
-What?

471
00:31:43,750 --> 00:31:46,708
It's just a prayer
that us loan-sharks do.

472
00:31:46,958 --> 00:31:48,583
You have prayers for cheating as well?

473
00:31:49,708 --> 00:31:51,250
Okay then! Carry on!

474
00:31:54,250 --> 00:31:55,917
Look who's here! Leelamma!

475
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:00,542
I'll sort this out.

476
00:32:00,875 --> 00:32:02,792
-Your husband is still in Dubai, right?
-No. He's at home.

477
00:32:02,958 --> 00:32:05,958
Is that so? Why did he come back?

478
00:32:06,667 --> 00:32:08,917
Shout! Shout! Shout loudly!

479
00:32:09,167 --> 00:32:12,542
Your throats will get sore,
but this Uthup will not resign!

480
00:32:12,667 --> 00:32:14,792
-Resign, you shameless fellow.
-Long Live!

481
00:32:14,958 --> 00:32:17,125
-Resign, man!
-That was awesome.

482
00:32:17,958 --> 00:32:20,042
Who's this? Hey, man!

483
00:32:20,167 --> 00:32:23,500
If it's about the club, it won't happen!
You have only two weeks more.

484
00:32:24,125 --> 00:32:26,667
-Get down from the Jeep.
-It's okay. I'm safe.

485
00:32:27,083 --> 00:32:28,667
-It's not about the club.
-Then?

486
00:32:28,875 --> 00:32:32,208
-About your marriage. Stella!
-Stella? What's happening?

487
00:32:33,167 --> 00:32:34,833
Did you talk to her?

488
00:32:35,083 --> 00:32:37,917
Shajiyettan put in a lot of effort
and trouble to make her agree.

489
00:32:38,125 --> 00:32:40,792
But how do we talk about this
without having a couple of drinks?

490
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:44,000
-Shall we drink?
-Not just a couple! Let's have four!

491
00:32:44,125 --> 00:32:48,083
-I am going crazy with happiness, Pappan!
-Even for us!

492
00:32:48,167 --> 00:32:50,333
Let's do one thing then.
Let's go to our bar.

493
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:54,917
Uthup sir, awesome!

494
00:32:56,917 --> 00:32:58,375
-Enough?
-Shall I fix one more?

495
00:32:58,667 --> 00:33:00,875
Enough. Six drinks is my limit.

496
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:03,458
And I don't like people who drink
without control.

497
00:33:03,792 --> 00:33:05,042
Tell me the matter.

498
00:33:06,042 --> 00:33:08,875
Even though she's slightly sad,
she finally agreed.

499
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:12,667
-Why does she have to be sad?
-Well, she's saying...

500
00:33:13,375 --> 00:33:15,042
-Or no need.
-Tell me, man!

501
00:33:15,292 --> 00:33:16,292
You tell him!

502
00:33:16,792 --> 00:33:19,583
For everything, that Antony
will be with you, right?

503
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:21,000
To drive, you need Antony.

504
00:33:21,458 --> 00:33:25,083
So people are saying that it's because
you're not able to do anything at all,

505
00:33:25,208 --> 00:33:28,167
you're taking Antony around
for help everywhere.

506
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:29,875
These are young kids, right?

507
00:33:30,083 --> 00:33:33,208
They are interested in people
who drive at 100 to 110 speed.

508
00:33:33,750 --> 00:33:36,875
Not just that. When you go
on your honeymoon after the wedding,

509
00:33:37,042 --> 00:33:39,875
would that girl doubt that this Antony
would be under the blanket?

510
00:33:40,167 --> 00:33:41,667
-He will do that.
-That's true!

511
00:33:41,917 --> 00:33:44,833
Some drivers can't be trusted.
Look at my case!

512
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:47,292
That scoundrel came to drive my car.
He left with my wife!

513
00:33:47,417 --> 00:33:48,750
He even stole the underwear I was wearing.

514
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:51,708
At least, Pappan had engine complaint.
But are you like him?

515
00:33:51,917 --> 00:33:53,833
-You're older than Pappan, right?
-That's true.

516
00:33:55,208 --> 00:33:57,833
-Have you heard that old is gold?
-I've heard of rolled gold.

517
00:33:57,958 --> 00:33:59,917
I'll show you now. Move!

518
00:34:00,542 --> 00:34:05,292
I have to shine in front of them.
They're trying to scare me.

519
00:34:05,458 --> 00:34:07,708
You went alone and boozed
without taking me?

520
00:34:09,958 --> 00:34:11,500
I have dismissed you!

521
00:34:15,167 --> 00:34:16,417
-Hey Cleetus!
-Yes?

522
00:34:16,625 --> 00:34:19,917
What did you say?
That I need someone for help?

523
00:34:20,083 --> 00:34:23,292
-Didn't Abu say that?
-Turn your mobile on if you want.

524
00:34:23,500 --> 00:34:27,542
And then go and show it to her
and tell her, that her groom is 'that'.

525
00:34:27,750 --> 00:34:31,250
-That?
-Yeah. The kids say it these days, right?

526
00:34:31,458 --> 00:34:35,917
What's that? Deadly! That's it!
Come on! Ready! Start!

527
00:34:44,417 --> 00:34:46,792
Move! Everyone move!

528
00:34:47,500 --> 00:34:49,042
Sixer!

529
00:34:49,333 --> 00:34:50,833
-Shall I buy a wreath?
-Wait.

530
00:34:51,125 --> 00:34:53,042
Shajiyetta, now it's become truly deadly!

531
00:34:54,125 --> 00:34:56,292
-Come, boys!
-He wants to mess with our club!

532
00:34:56,583 --> 00:35:00,083
<i>Anangappara Panchayat President,</i>
<i>Mr. Uthup Thekkepparambil was arrested.</i>

533
00:35:00,208 --> 00:35:02,375
<i>He tried to disrupt</i>
<i>the opposition's strike,</i>

534
00:35:02,458 --> 00:35:05,625
<i>by driving his Jeep into the middle of the</i>
<i>strike, under the influence of alcohol.</i>

535
00:35:05,708 --> 00:35:08,000
<i>As people ran away, a grave</i>
<i>disaster was avoided.</i>

536
00:35:08,083 --> 00:35:09,208
My God!

537
00:35:09,917 --> 00:35:14,083
-What happened to President Uthup?
-Can't keep it in his pants!

538
00:35:17,167 --> 00:35:19,417
-This is so spicy!
-What?

539
00:35:19,875 --> 00:35:22,167
Nothing. If I say something,
you'll add poison to this.

540
00:35:23,417 --> 00:35:26,625
-Where is this from?
-Jackfruit dish. Stella Chechi made it.

541
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:28,500
<i>No Pappan</i>

542
00:35:28,875 --> 00:35:30,625
<i>She'll cheat you, Pappan</i>

543
00:35:30,750 --> 00:35:31,750
Very nice.

544
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:34,667
It's not so nice. It's too spicy.
And there's too much of cumin.

545
00:35:36,375 --> 00:35:38,125
I've liked the spice since yesterday.

546
00:35:41,708 --> 00:35:43,792
You hit me with the bowl
on my head, right? It's still hurting!

547
00:35:44,417 --> 00:35:47,583
I was looking for a shovel. You're lucky
that I only got that bowl in my hand.

548
00:35:48,875 --> 00:35:52,333
-I'm going to sell her. Do you want her?
-He wants to mortgage our house documents!

549
00:35:52,458 --> 00:35:54,792
-You could've given it, right?
-She will kill me with these curses.

550
00:35:57,000 --> 00:36:00,625
God! Is there be anyone in this world
who's more hopeless than me?

551
00:36:19,042 --> 00:36:22,292
-What's your name?
-Paily. Dragon Paily.

552
00:36:22,458 --> 00:36:25,375
-You were the one who named me, Dude Sir.
-Such a lousy name!

553
00:36:25,708 --> 00:36:26,792
Sheesh!

554
00:36:38,125 --> 00:36:40,833
-The bananas would've fallen now.
-My banana was crushed.

555
00:36:43,542 --> 00:36:44,875
What? No money?

556
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:46,708
That's what my brother said, sir.

557
00:36:47,375 --> 00:36:49,917
Did you think that I'm a <i>Vahanam</i>
that comes for free?

558
00:36:50,042 --> 00:36:51,708
I'm the <i>Vahanam </i>that collects money!

559
00:36:51,917 --> 00:36:54,375
The name is Mayilvahanam!
Go ask him,

560
00:36:54,708 --> 00:36:58,625
does he need his hands to cut vegetables,
or not? Get going!

561
00:36:59,333 --> 00:37:03,792
-<i>Salaam Alaikum</i>, Sulaimaan!
-<i>Wa Alaikum Salaam</i>! What is it, sir?

562
00:37:04,333 --> 00:37:06,208
Stay there. I will come there.

563
00:37:07,750 --> 00:37:11,000
Maan, Maan! Haven't I told you
a thousand times?

564
00:37:11,167 --> 00:37:15,458
That if you go to the market, don't dawdle
around too much, and come back fast?

565
00:37:15,625 --> 00:37:16,625
Yes.

566
00:37:19,458 --> 00:37:21,708
What happened to him? Brother, is he dead?

567
00:37:21,917 --> 00:37:23,958
He'll kill everyone around him!

568
00:37:24,083 --> 00:37:26,125
Clean the dishes and start making
<i>parottas</i>! Go!

569
00:37:27,708 --> 00:37:28,875
Take your cap as well!

570
00:37:28,958 --> 00:37:31,125
Where is the dough?
The dough is missing!

571
00:37:31,875 --> 00:37:33,833
Malayalis ask for work first,

572
00:37:33,917 --> 00:37:36,958
and once we give them the job,
they try to work against us!

573
00:37:37,583 --> 00:37:40,083
You continue eating.
This is all entertainment.

574
00:37:40,208 --> 00:37:41,917
Two <i>parottas </i>a piece, please!

575
00:37:43,583 --> 00:37:44,875
My fate!

576
00:37:45,333 --> 00:37:46,417
-Dude sir.
-Yes!

577
00:37:46,500 --> 00:37:47,542
-Dude sir.
-Yes!

578
00:37:47,625 --> 00:37:48,708
Give some of that.

579
00:37:55,708 --> 00:37:57,208
Was this his actual job?

580
00:37:57,292 --> 00:37:59,708
There's no water in the pipe.
We have to get it from the well.

581
00:37:59,917 --> 00:38:02,667
Dude, why do you need to do this?

582
00:38:02,833 --> 00:38:06,292
Shall we put him nicely into that stove
and escape, Dude?

583
00:38:06,458 --> 00:38:07,458
And go where?

584
00:38:07,917 --> 00:38:10,958
We came looking for the <i>neelakoduveli</i>
herb, and boss died over there.

585
00:38:11,292 --> 00:38:13,500
If we go to Bangkok now,
they will shoot us to death!

586
00:38:14,333 --> 00:38:15,750
And if we leave to Kerala,

587
00:38:16,083 --> 00:38:18,750
-Kerala Police will bash us up like crazy.
-Definitely!

588
00:38:20,625 --> 00:38:23,458
So until this operation is over,
this will be our base.

589
00:38:24,542 --> 00:38:25,917
Understood, Mr. Bull Paily?

590
00:38:26,042 --> 00:38:27,958
-Dragon Paily!
-Whatever Paily it is!

591
00:38:28,125 --> 00:38:30,375
You're the one who introduced
me to that ganja, Soman

592
00:38:30,458 --> 00:38:31,542
and that's when this started.

593
00:38:35,958 --> 00:38:38,167
-I'm lucky that he didn't have his gun.
<i>-What's the noise there?</i>

594
00:38:38,292 --> 00:38:41,625
Nothing, sir. I was just talking
to the dishes and cleaning them!

595
00:38:45,083 --> 00:38:46,417
-Come here, man!
-Coming!

596
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:49,000
What is this?

597
00:38:50,875 --> 00:38:52,333
-Come here, man!
-Coming!

598
00:38:58,333 --> 00:38:59,333
You scared me!

599
00:39:03,958 --> 00:39:05,042
Don't make noise.

600
00:39:09,042 --> 00:39:11,875
BANK OF TAMIL NADU

601
00:39:13,417 --> 00:39:15,208
Slice him to death! Go!

602
00:39:18,292 --> 00:39:19,458
Maan!

603
00:39:19,875 --> 00:39:22,333
Nothing, sir.
This dough is a little tight.

604
00:39:22,542 --> 00:39:24,750
Only Dude sir can beat
him at his own game!

605
00:39:25,458 --> 00:39:28,083
Don't get me in trouble.
Make <i>parottas</i>, you idiot!

606
00:39:36,917 --> 00:39:41,167
<i>Excitement builds up like fire</i>

607
00:39:41,375 --> 00:39:44,000
<i>All over our nerves</i>

608
00:39:44,125 --> 00:39:46,708
Pappan! We got a new guy
instead of Rohith!

609
00:39:47,125 --> 00:39:49,458
-Who is this?
-He plays very well.

610
00:39:49,583 --> 00:39:51,708
Let me see your hand.
And your legs?

611
00:39:53,542 --> 00:39:54,792
We'll sort you out. Go!

612
00:39:54,875 --> 00:39:56,542
<i>There's a lightning in my heart</i>

613
00:39:56,625 --> 00:39:58,708
<i>The heart is providing the rhythm</i>

614
00:39:59,833 --> 00:40:01,792
What are you doing there?
Throw this mud away!

615
00:40:01,875 --> 00:40:03,083
What is this, man?

616
00:40:03,292 --> 00:40:05,333
<i>There are many friends for company</i>

617
00:40:05,458 --> 00:40:07,708
<i>We are progressing together</i>

618
00:40:07,833 --> 00:40:12,083
<i>Let's go forward</i>
<i>With the speed of the wind, my friend</i>

619
00:40:12,292 --> 00:40:14,500
<i>Excitement builds up like fire</i>

620
00:40:14,625 --> 00:40:15,500
HONDA ACTIVA WELFARE FUND

621
00:40:16,833 --> 00:40:21,083
<i>All over our nerves</i>

622
00:40:21,375 --> 00:40:25,417
<i>With vigor, without losing focus</i>

623
00:40:25,750 --> 00:40:30,375
<i>We are searching for new paths</i>

624
00:40:30,708 --> 00:40:34,167
I'm getting bored of counting this!
Maan!

625
00:40:34,542 --> 00:40:35,833
-Sulaimaan!
-Yes sir.

626
00:40:36,333 --> 00:40:38,583
-Come here, darling.
-You want tea?

627
00:40:39,458 --> 00:40:42,708
-They have raised the tax at Walayar.
-Is that even a reason, sir?

628
00:40:42,917 --> 00:40:44,833
It's 300 kilometers away from here.

629
00:40:44,958 --> 00:40:46,750
I feel like slapping you
whenever I see you.

630
00:40:46,917 --> 00:40:49,667
Hey! All this is entertainment!
Get lost!

631
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:51,500
Go do your work!
Maan!

632
00:40:52,167 --> 00:40:53,833
Did they raise the tax anywhere else?

633
00:40:57,083 --> 00:41:01,042
<i>Matching each other's steps,</i>
<i>Without faltering</i>

634
00:41:01,417 --> 00:41:05,583
<i>Don't step back, whatever happens</i>
<i>Keep going forward</i>

635
00:41:05,792 --> 00:41:10,167
<i>There are many stairs</i>
<i>Throughout the path</i>

636
00:41:10,250 --> 00:41:14,333
<i>Don't retreat</i>
<i>Go forward together with vigor</i>

637
00:41:14,583 --> 00:41:16,750
<i>If this works out, you'll have</i>
<i>A fortune in hand</i>

638
00:41:16,875 --> 00:41:19,083
<i>If not, what could happen?</i>

639
00:41:19,208 --> 00:41:23,083
<i>Let us just try once</i>
<i>Come on</i>

640
00:41:23,500 --> 00:41:27,708
<i>Like a flame of light, you should be</i>
<i>All over the path, leading me</i>

641
00:41:27,917 --> 00:41:32,417
<i>Always with me, as my strength</i>

642
00:41:33,833 --> 00:41:35,292
Bro, mud is falling on my face.

643
00:41:35,417 --> 00:41:36,417
-What?
-Mud.

644
00:41:36,875 --> 00:41:38,417
-On your face?
-Yeah.

645
00:41:39,792 --> 00:41:44,667
I sold the car I had, and bought bermudas
to go to Bangkok, and this is my fate.

646
00:41:45,000 --> 00:41:46,458
And you have a problem
with some mud?

647
00:41:46,542 --> 00:41:48,542
If you talk again,
I will hit your head with this!

648
00:41:48,875 --> 00:41:49,750
Okay! Dig!

649
00:41:50,250 --> 00:41:53,917
<i>Excitement builds up like fire</i>

650
00:41:54,042 --> 00:41:56,375
<i>All over our nerves</i>

651
00:41:59,042 --> 00:42:00,500
What's up, sir? Do you want tea?

652
00:42:00,625 --> 00:42:03,125
Play with your own kind! Get lost!

653
00:42:07,667 --> 00:42:09,667
<i>There's a lightning in my heart</i>

654
00:42:09,792 --> 00:42:12,083
<i>The heart is providing the rhythm</i>

655
00:42:12,167 --> 00:42:16,042
<i>To achieve our goal</i>
<i>We don't have to travel far</i>

656
00:42:16,417 --> 00:42:18,417
<i>There are many friends for company</i>

657
00:42:18,542 --> 00:42:20,583
<i>We are progressing together</i>

658
00:42:20,958 --> 00:42:24,125
<i>Let's go forward</i>
<i>With the speed of the wind, my friend</i>

659
00:42:24,208 --> 00:42:25,375
"IDUKKI IS SHINING" RALLY

660
00:42:25,792 --> 00:42:27,542
<i>Excitement builds up like fire</i>

661
00:42:27,625 --> 00:42:28,625
Some--

662
00:42:28,958 --> 00:42:30,708
-Some salt.
-Maan!

663
00:42:31,042 --> 00:42:33,208
What is it, sir? Omelet is ready!

664
00:42:33,708 --> 00:42:36,625
-You come here.
-Me? Coming, sir.

665
00:42:37,208 --> 00:42:38,292
What is it, sir?

666
00:42:41,083 --> 00:42:42,167
What was this for?

667
00:42:42,333 --> 00:42:44,292
If I had a joker, I would have hit
a jackpot.

668
00:42:44,417 --> 00:42:45,750
That's why I hit you.

669
00:42:47,042 --> 00:42:48,917
My darling!
All this is entertainment, man!

670
00:42:49,042 --> 00:42:50,750
On my face? Entertainment?

671
00:42:51,375 --> 00:42:52,792
-Now you may go.
-I'll show you.

672
00:42:53,375 --> 00:42:54,708
Okay. Stay blessed.

673
00:42:55,875 --> 00:42:58,667
-Is Paily Vattakkuzhi here?
-Sir, he's at the backside.

674
00:43:00,333 --> 00:43:02,750
-This isn't working.
-Cut the opposite side, you monkey!

675
00:43:03,917 --> 00:43:05,417
-Dude sir, one doubt.
-Yes.

676
00:43:05,500 --> 00:43:07,125
Have you ever looked at your face
in a mirror?

677
