<i>I'm a flower that turns shy</i>
<i>With the touch of a finger</i>

1065
01:08:42,750 --> 01:08:47,417
<i>I saw a rosy dream in a cold cozy night</i>

1066
01:08:47,833 --> 01:08:50,208
<i>Oh, naughty girl</i>

1067
01:08:50,333 --> 01:08:55,167
<i>Won't you set my heart on fire?</i>

1068
01:08:57,875 --> 01:09:04,833
<i>This style of mine, and my entire youth</i>
<i>It's all for you, my king</i>

1069
01:09:05,625 --> 01:09:12,583
<i>I'm at the prime of my youth</i>
<i>I can't bear it any longer, come on</i>

1070
01:09:13,250 --> 01:09:16,542
<i>Don't look at me like that</i>
<i>With your lovely eyes</i>

1071
01:09:16,625 --> 01:09:20,750
<i>And send thunderstorms in my heart</i>

1072
01:09:20,917 --> 01:09:27,875
<i>This body of mine is electrified</i>
<i>Come to me, my dear</i>

1073
01:09:43,458 --> 01:09:44,792
Stop it!

1074
01:09:54,375 --> 01:09:55,792
This is Shaji Pappan.

1075
01:09:56,708 --> 01:10:00,042
From the High Range.
The cup that you stole from us...

1076
01:10:01,208 --> 01:10:02,583
I've come here to take it back.

1077
01:10:03,750 --> 01:10:07,042
That's right! You will take
a lot back from here.

1078
01:10:09,125 --> 01:10:12,750
This, this is my brother, Lassar,
the devil's place!

1079
01:10:17,042 --> 01:10:19,042
You little viper, Sabu...

1080
01:10:20,083 --> 01:10:22,917
even if your dead brother, Lassar,
the devil,

1081
01:10:23,542 --> 01:10:25,833
even if his father, Lucifer Mathan, comes,

1082
01:10:26,875 --> 01:10:29,542
-Pappan will still leave with the cup!
-Then try taking it!

1083
01:10:33,708 --> 01:10:35,042
Awesome, Shajiyetta!

1084
01:10:38,167 --> 01:10:39,708
My back isn't sprained. Thank God.

1085
01:10:43,125 --> 01:10:46,875
<i>Even Haji Mastan would salute</i>
<i>The brave and mighty Shaji Pappan</i>

1086
01:10:46,958 --> 01:10:50,792
<i>Even an atom bomb would defuse</i>
<i>On its own at the sight of Shaji Pappan</i>

1087
01:10:54,333 --> 01:10:55,833
Are they going to swim?

1088
01:10:55,917 --> 01:10:57,667
This is what happens
if you mess with Pappan!

1089
01:10:57,833 --> 01:10:59,917
Why does he sound like that?

1090
01:11:00,208 --> 01:11:01,750
Put them on properly. Turn them around.

1091
01:11:09,708 --> 01:11:12,667
Moonga! Take out the tools!

1092
01:11:24,625 --> 01:11:26,292
Beat these pigs to death!

1093
01:11:30,583 --> 01:11:32,375
Cleetus, throw the next ball!

1094
01:11:32,625 --> 01:11:35,125
<i>The festival is off to a grand start</i>
<i>There's euphoria all around</i>

1095
01:11:35,292 --> 01:11:37,667
<i>A team of warriors has arrived</i>
<i>To win tug of war with vigor</i>

1096
01:11:37,792 --> 01:11:41,375
<i>Accompanied with trunks and trumpets</i>
<i>And drum beats praising them</i>

1097
01:11:41,458 --> 01:11:44,000
<i>With courage in their words and actions</i>

1098
01:11:49,167 --> 01:11:50,042
Come!

1099
01:11:50,458 --> 01:11:56,208
<i>Even the whole world will crumble</i>
<i>At their hands</i>

1100
01:11:56,333 --> 01:12:02,042
<i>To reach the sky as a lightning</i>
<i>Their mighty hearts find fresh paths</i>

1101
01:12:30,083 --> 01:12:31,292
Come here, you fatso!

1102
01:12:32,875 --> 01:12:33,875
Catch me!

1103
01:12:36,208 --> 01:12:37,833
Sorry, Chechi. That guy is quite shady.

1104
01:12:38,500 --> 01:12:40,583
Look at you standing there!
But I'm decent, okay!

1105
01:13:09,708 --> 01:13:11,542
This is a flag hoisted by Shaji Pappan!

1106
01:13:12,833 --> 01:13:14,625
Hereafter, there won't be
any dance bar here...

1107
01:13:16,125 --> 01:13:17,917
or whatever the fuck happens here.

1108
01:13:24,583 --> 01:13:25,750
Come!

1109
01:13:27,917 --> 01:13:29,917
-Pappan, I'll be right back.
-Where is he going?

1110
01:13:37,292 --> 01:13:39,792
Come, Pappan. I've written
our full address and phone number.

1111
01:13:39,875 --> 01:13:41,667
Let everyone know that we did this!

1112
01:13:42,208 --> 01:13:43,208
That's good.

1113
01:13:43,333 --> 01:13:48,958
<i>Even the whole world will crumble</i>
<i>At their hands</i>

1114
01:13:49,042 --> 01:13:54,708
<i>To reach the sky as a lightning</i>
<i>Their mighty hearts find fresh paths</i>

1115
01:14:00,208 --> 01:14:01,375
Who are these people, sir?

1116
01:14:01,500 --> 01:14:04,500
The one sitting on this side
on the left wing is Battery Simon.

1117
01:14:04,667 --> 01:14:06,042
He used to brew arrack.

1118
01:14:06,708 --> 01:14:08,917
The one next to him is Ganja Soman.

1119
01:14:09,500 --> 01:14:13,583
When both their businesses were caught,
they started working as Satan's sidekicks.

1120
01:14:14,333 --> 01:14:16,333
A big deal is happening here
for Satan today.

1121
01:14:16,542 --> 01:14:18,542
It's some Dubai underworld
on the other side.

1122
01:14:19,042 --> 01:14:22,083
Why are we sitting here while the deal
is happening when we could be sleeping?

1123
01:14:22,792 --> 01:14:25,000
You fool! I will teach you today,

1124
01:14:25,542 --> 01:14:28,458
how to catch an underworld deal,
red-handed!

1125
01:14:29,292 --> 01:14:31,667
-Govindan, you also watch carefully.
-Okay, sir.

1126
01:14:34,542 --> 01:14:37,708
-Yes. Blue Carbuncle. It's original.
-Good.

1127
01:14:38,167 --> 01:14:40,792
Satan Xavier deals only original stuff!

1128
01:14:41,333 --> 01:14:42,875
-Isn't that so?
-Yes. Of course!

1129
01:14:43,000 --> 01:14:44,917
So we've brought the full amount
you asked for.

1130
01:14:45,125 --> 01:14:48,042
Sir, they are about to close the deal.
Shall we jump in and catch them?

1131
01:14:48,208 --> 01:14:51,542
No. While catching a snake,
we have to hit it on its head!

1132
01:14:51,708 --> 01:14:53,083
-Let him come.
-Who?

1133
01:14:53,208 --> 01:14:54,542
Satan Xavier.

1134
01:14:55,625 --> 01:14:58,250
When I jump in and catch him,
you should take a photo.

1135
01:14:58,375 --> 01:14:59,417
That's what this camera is for.

1136
01:14:59,542 --> 01:15:01,250
-Okay then.
-Wait a second.

1137
01:15:02,792 --> 01:15:06,042
Once this deal is over, we will be
back in Dubai in no time.

1138
01:15:06,125 --> 01:15:07,583
Then you will never be able to find us.

1139
01:15:07,708 --> 01:15:09,167
-I didn't understand.
-Simple.

1140
01:15:09,667 --> 01:15:13,792
Xavier, who sent two country bumpkins
like you for this deal, is a bigger fool!

1141
01:15:14,083 --> 01:15:16,583
If you leave now,
you can at least stay alive.

1142
01:15:16,958 --> 01:15:19,208
Don't speak about the cash or diamonds.

1143
01:15:19,542 --> 01:15:21,875
-Get going. Fast!
-No, sir.

1144
01:15:22,083 --> 01:15:24,042
Satan Xavier would never forgive betrayal.

1145
01:15:24,167 --> 01:15:26,833
You won't ever leave the High Range
after cheating Satan Xavier.

1146
01:15:27,708 --> 01:15:30,000
Then call your Satan Xavier.

1147
01:15:37,333 --> 01:15:38,417
-Take it.
-Sir.

1148
01:15:39,250 --> 01:15:42,042
-Sir, food.
-But we didn't order any food.

1149
01:15:42,458 --> 01:15:44,833
Stupid! Food, is this a hotel?

1150
01:15:45,292 --> 01:15:48,667
-What is this?
-Satan Xavier ordered this for you.

1151
01:15:51,833 --> 01:15:53,458
Sir, food has been served.

1152
01:15:53,583 --> 01:15:55,583
We also could have ordered
two parottas, right?

1153
01:15:58,167 --> 01:15:59,500
Must be fried chicken.

1154
01:16:05,583 --> 01:16:07,292
<i>That you could escape from here</i>

1155
01:16:07,375 --> 01:16:09,250
<i>with the cash and diamond</i>
<i>by cheating Xavier?</i>

1156
01:16:09,750 --> 01:16:14,250
<i>You are terribly mistaken.</i>
<i>Satan Xavier never forgives betrayal!</i>

1157
01:16:14,500 --> 01:16:16,917
<i>When this call is cut,</i>
<i>that bomb will explode.</i>

1158
01:16:17,042 --> 01:16:19,792
<i>My two sidekicks may also explode</i>
<i>into pieces along with you.</i>

1159
01:16:20,000 --> 01:16:23,625
-God!
<i>-But I don't care! So what do you think?</i>

1160
01:16:24,125 --> 01:16:26,458
<i>-Do you want to explode, or not?</i>
-Step back.

1161
01:16:26,583 --> 01:16:27,958
Sir, bomb!

1162
01:16:29,208 --> 01:16:30,333
-Dhanaya...
-Yes.

1163
01:16:30,750 --> 01:16:32,792
-...are you afraid?
-Completely, sir.

1164
01:16:33,792 --> 01:16:36,667
-Then run through the fields.
-What about you?

1165
01:16:37,375 --> 01:16:40,333
-Don't wait for me. Take him as well.
-He left a while back!

1166
01:16:46,375 --> 01:16:48,125
It will blow up now.
He doesn't know how to count!

1167
01:16:48,667 --> 01:16:52,125
<i>-...six, five, four, three...</i>
-Catch it.

1168
01:16:53,458 --> 01:16:56,250
<i>-Good boy.</i>
-Wait there. I'll be right back.

1169
01:16:59,000 --> 01:17:02,167
You know what that is for?
For trying to kill us with this bomb!

1170
01:17:02,292 --> 01:17:04,125
You and your coat. Take off your pants.

1171
01:17:04,250 --> 01:17:08,167
You only need a mundu. Take it off.
You're trying to mess with Satan Xavier?

1172
01:17:09,125 --> 01:17:10,875
Come!

1173
01:17:22,125 --> 01:17:25,917
<i>The highly dangerous underworld</i>
<i>Kingpin of the High Range</i>

1174
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:29,083
<i>Like a high voltage thunderbolt</i>

1175
01:17:29,542 --> 01:17:35,833
<i>Satan Xavier</i>

1176
01:17:36,917 --> 01:17:43,333
<i>Satan Xavier</i>
<i>Satan Xavier</i>

1177
01:17:44,333 --> 01:17:48,083
<i>The highly dangerous underworld</i>
<i>Kingpin of the High Range</i>

1178
01:17:48,167 --> 01:17:50,750
<i>Like a high voltage thunderbolt</i>

1179
01:18:00,125 --> 01:18:01,125
Boss!

1180
01:18:01,458 --> 01:18:04,667
When you said it was a bomb, they peed
in their pants and gave us all the money!

1181
01:18:04,750 --> 01:18:06,667
They peed? I didn't see that.

1182
01:18:06,917 --> 01:18:10,042
-I said that for a punchline.
-Then shall we?

1183
01:18:12,042 --> 01:18:15,125
Work on the field, wage at the ledge.

1184
01:18:15,625 --> 01:18:19,125
That's Satan's policy. Spend it carefully.

1185
01:18:20,458 --> 01:18:23,000
Deposit some in the bank as well.
Then get going!

1186
01:18:24,667 --> 01:18:28,458
-A thousand rupees?
-Such a nice man!

1187
01:18:28,583 --> 01:18:31,000
Then you go and light candles
at his father's grave.

1188
01:18:31,083 --> 01:18:32,750
One thousand plus one thousand
makes two thousand.

1189
01:18:32,833 --> 01:18:34,000
Will the GST guys catch me?

1190
01:18:44,625 --> 01:18:46,625
-Use the gas-cutter carefully.
-Yes, sir.

1191
01:18:46,833 --> 01:18:48,042
Once you enter the room,

1192
01:18:48,208 --> 01:18:50,292
-you should cut the locker immediately.
-Okay.

1193
01:18:50,667 --> 01:18:52,750
And at midnight,
we should burn this hotel down,

1194
01:18:53,375 --> 01:18:56,917
break that Tamilian's head
and leave the country with the money.

1195
01:18:57,042 --> 01:18:58,708
Aren't you coming to take money
from the locker, dude, sir?

1196
01:18:58,792 --> 01:19:01,583
No! I've to cut onions
for an egg roast tomorrow.

1197
01:19:01,708 --> 01:19:05,167
You contact me on the wireless, okay?
One second.

1198
01:19:06,500 --> 01:19:08,875
I've been planning this for six months.
Don't screw it up!

1199
01:19:10,042 --> 01:19:11,292
Come on!

1200
01:19:20,625 --> 01:19:22,292
<i>Cobra! Cobra!</i>

1201
01:19:31,042 --> 01:19:35,375
It's three-three-three, you fool! Hello?

1202
01:20:04,667 --> 01:20:07,208
-I got in okay.
-Well done, my boy! Well done!

1203
01:20:07,500 --> 01:20:08,792
-I'm going to start work.
-Yes.

1204
01:20:55,667 --> 01:20:57,208
-Dude, sir!
-Have you opened the locker?

1205
01:20:57,583 --> 01:21:01,417
Yes. I think we're really lucky.
They are all 500s and 1000s.

1206
01:21:01,583 --> 01:21:04,000
No 100s or 50s!
Not even one bundle.

1207
01:21:08,417 --> 01:21:11,958
I will cut you like I'm cutting
these onions, you Mayilvahanam!

1208
01:21:12,417 --> 01:21:15,500
<i>Money! Money! Money!</i>

1209
01:21:15,833 --> 01:21:19,500
I don't know what I'm going to do
with so much money!

1210
01:21:21,458 --> 01:21:22,500
<i>-Today...</i>
-Yes.

1211
01:21:22,625 --> 01:21:23,667
<i>...from midnight...</i>

1212
01:21:24,250 --> 01:21:28,250
-Tell me, my Prime Minister! Tell me!
<i>-...means, Eighth November, 2016...</i>

1213
01:21:29,792 --> 01:21:31,750
<i>from midnight 12 AM,</i>

1214
01:21:32,167 --> 01:21:37,458
<i>the currency notes</i>
<i>of 500 rupees and 1000 rupees...</i>

1215
01:21:39,417 --> 01:21:42,333
<i>will cease to be legal tender.</i>

1216
01:22:13,167 --> 01:22:15,208
Dragon, don't take anything.
Come back fast.

1217
01:22:19,625 --> 01:22:20,625
Dude...

1218
01:22:25,333 --> 01:22:26,333
Don't wait any longer.

1219
01:22:27,500 --> 01:22:29,333
-Start!
-Okay, boss.

1220
01:22:37,667 --> 01:22:41,542
-Sulaimaan, what's that noise there?
-Nothing, boss.

1221
01:22:41,667 --> 01:22:44,875
I'm mixing the dough by talking to it!

1222
01:23:09,583 --> 01:23:12,292
Sreesanth is innocent!

1223
01:23:12,375 --> 01:23:14,375
-Are you crazy?
-Don't interfere with this, Sachin!

1224
01:23:14,958 --> 01:23:17,583
I'll give you one tight slap!
He's talking in his sleep!

1225
01:23:18,125 --> 01:23:21,542
-Has he lost his senses full time or what?
-Shajiyetta,

1226
01:23:21,667 --> 01:23:24,750
we should definitely take Cleetus
to a gynecologist tomorrow.

1227
01:23:25,000 --> 01:23:28,083
-That might be necessary.
-Don't sleep anymore.

1228
01:23:28,583 --> 01:23:31,792
We've reached. Hey!
You can leave with the van.

1229
01:23:32,292 --> 01:23:35,333
-Bring it tomorrow.
-Didn't Vidya Balan get in the van?

1230
01:23:35,792 --> 01:23:36,958
-What?
-What's that?

1231
01:23:37,125 --> 01:23:39,042
Did they move the church festival
to my house?

1232
01:23:39,833 --> 01:23:42,208
-Pappan, what is that?
-What is this?

1233
01:23:42,333 --> 01:23:43,333
It's burning.

1234
01:23:43,458 --> 01:23:44,875
-God, what is this?
-Get down!

1235
01:23:45,000 --> 01:23:47,333
Hey! It's him! Isn't that him?

1236
01:23:47,875 --> 01:23:49,625
It's Diwali at Pappan's house?

1237
01:23:52,292 --> 01:23:53,833
Didn't you get enough?

1238
01:23:58,458 --> 01:24:01,667
I will slice you all into pieces tonight!

1239
01:24:02,000 --> 01:24:04,417
Moonga! Get me the stuff!

1240
01:24:04,833 --> 01:24:07,125
-Blast it, Pappan!
-Come up here, man!

1241
01:24:08,500 --> 01:24:09,375
I'm coming!

1242
01:24:22,208 --> 01:24:24,250
All of us can explode together!

1243
01:24:24,833 --> 01:24:29,208
If I die in a bomb explosion,
Pappan doesn't care!

1244
01:25:12,333 --> 01:25:14,750
-What is that? A flag post?
-I don't know!

1245
01:25:22,917 --> 01:25:24,583
What's this? Is a coconut tree walking?

1246
01:25:40,417 --> 01:25:43,750
Lassar. Lassar, the devil.

1247
01:25:44,292 --> 01:25:48,208
Lassar doesn't care
if that bomb explodes.

1248
01:25:51,417 --> 01:25:53,000
This isn't a bomb.

1249
01:25:54,125 --> 01:25:56,875
You died in a bomb blast, right?

1250
01:25:57,208 --> 01:25:59,750
-That was the rumor.
-Pappan!

1251
01:26:00,333 --> 01:26:02,250
Jump and punch him in the face!

1252
01:26:02,417 --> 01:26:05,000
-Finish him, Shajiyetta!
-Don't talk like that.

1253
01:26:06,583 --> 01:26:08,958
I didn't even die when a bomb exploded!

1254
01:26:09,375 --> 01:26:11,583
And you're trying to scare me
with a firecracker?

1255
01:26:23,458 --> 01:26:25,792
-Are we in trouble?
-I needn't interfere.

1256
01:26:41,208 --> 01:26:42,375
Don't do it, sir.

1257
01:26:45,375 --> 01:26:48,917
It's good that you wrote down your
address when you hoisted that flag.

1258
01:26:49,125 --> 01:26:50,958
-It was easy getting here.
-Escape!

1259
01:26:51,042 --> 01:26:55,333
You destroyed my building,
the public broke in and stole my money...

1260
01:26:56,208 --> 01:26:58,000
and most of my goods were burnt.

1261
01:26:58,750 --> 01:27:01,208
I've written accounts
for all that in this. Here!

1262
01:27:01,417 --> 01:27:04,500
Twenty-seven-hundred-thousand! Jesus!

1263
01:27:06,250 --> 01:27:09,375
I want the full amount within two days.

1264
01:27:09,625 --> 01:27:12,125
And you have to go there
with the money.

1265
01:27:12,792 --> 01:27:14,792
Did you think Sabu
was just a proprietor

1266
01:27:14,917 --> 01:27:16,208
of a third-rate dance bar?

1267
01:27:27,667 --> 01:27:31,125
When did you guys get here?
There's tea in the kitchen.

1268
01:27:32,083 --> 01:27:35,500
-Serve tea for all of them, dear.
-Shajiyetta, you are not sleeping at home.

1269
01:27:35,583 --> 01:27:38,167
They beat you up, you lost your senses
and you're in the hospital now!

1270
01:27:38,292 --> 01:27:39,542
-Hospital?
-Yes.

1271
01:27:39,708 --> 01:27:41,667
-Yes. See these oranges?
-Pappan,

1272
01:27:42,333 --> 01:27:45,583
they took Bastin, Moonga
and our golden cup as well.

1273
01:27:46,167 --> 01:27:49,583
They took them? Even the cup? Jesus!

1274
01:27:50,583 --> 01:27:53,000
Will they hurt my boys?

1275
01:27:53,667 --> 01:27:56,417
Usually they run when something
like this happens, right?

1276
01:27:56,500 --> 01:27:58,583
They got scared seeing that devil
and were frozen.

1277
01:27:58,750 --> 01:28:00,292
-Jesus!
-Shajiyetta!

1278
01:28:00,542 --> 01:28:02,500
What do we do to make
that twenty-seven-hundred-thousand now?

1279
01:28:02,583 --> 01:28:04,167
-I don't know, man!
-Pappan,

1280
01:28:04,750 --> 01:28:06,875
-there's good news as well.
-What is it?

1281
01:28:07,708 --> 01:28:11,750
Our Prime Minister, right?
He banned all the 500 and 1000 notes!

1282
01:28:12,042 --> 01:28:15,208
-What?
-The 500 and 1000 notes are banned.

1283
01:28:19,250 --> 01:28:21,208
In between all the punches I got,

1284
01:28:21,417 --> 01:28:24,500
how did he have the heart
to ban the notes?

1285
01:28:25,333 --> 01:28:28,167
How do I make
twenty-seven-hundred-thousand, Jesus?

1286
01:28:29,958 --> 01:28:31,667
I have seen her somewhere.

1287
01:28:32,750 --> 01:28:34,292
Isn't that my mom? I was here?

1288
01:28:34,417 --> 01:28:37,500
You won't leave me in peace
here either, you devil?

1289
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:42,958
<i>When the dead Lassar, the Devil, rose</i>
<i>from the ashes and kicked his spine,</i>

1290
01:28:43,167 --> 01:28:44,583
<i>Pappan was in shock.</i>

1291
01:28:44,750 --> 01:28:49,000
<i>But the public was shocked</i>
<i>when the Prime Minister banned the notes.</i>

1292
01:28:49,125 --> 01:28:51,333
I've brought the money. Black!

1293
01:28:52,042 --> 01:28:53,500
Yes. 500s and 1000s.

1294
01:28:55,542 --> 01:28:58,708
Swearing at my dad? Why are you swearing
while talking about money?

1295
01:28:58,833 --> 01:29:00,458
-Dude, 500 and 1000 notes were banned!
-Who?

1296
01:29:00,583 --> 01:29:01,708
The Prime Minister.

1297
01:29:04,792 --> 01:29:09,000
Such high hopes we had!
Smuggling, bomb explosion,

1298
01:29:09,583 --> 01:29:11,833
we thought life would be much better,

1299
01:29:11,958 --> 01:29:14,292
now I'll have go back
to illegal arrack brewing again!

1300
01:29:14,583 --> 01:29:18,000
The police will beat me to death again!
I swear!

1301
01:29:24,542 --> 01:29:27,708
-Prabhakaran, what's happening?
-4.5 billion rupees, brother.

1302
01:29:27,833 --> 01:29:30,042
Make it fast.
We've got to send the load tonight.

1303
01:29:30,167 --> 01:29:35,417
<i>...one thousand rupees notes</i>
<i>will not be legal tender.</i>

1304
01:29:38,833 --> 01:29:40,458
-Prabhakara!
-Brother!

1305
01:29:40,625 --> 01:29:42,667
Even though it's meant to trick people
with fake money,

1306
01:29:42,750 --> 01:29:46,458
our fake-note printers
are in much more trouble now.

1307
01:29:46,542 --> 01:29:47,417
Yes.

1308
01:29:47,500 --> 01:29:49,750
I'll have to feed these printed notes
to some cow now, God!

1309
01:29:50,958 --> 01:29:52,833
Brother, call that Brother Suresh.

1310
01:29:53,167 --> 01:29:54,750
-Is that necessary?
-Yes.

1311
01:30:06,542 --> 01:30:07,417
Greetings, brother.

1312
01:30:13,375 --> 01:30:15,792
-Where is Shetty?
-He is inside.

1313
01:30:18,292 --> 01:30:21,417
My dear Shetty,
why are you getting tense?

1314
01:30:21,792 --> 01:30:23,833
This demonetization
is not such a big problem.

1315
01:30:24,000 --> 01:30:27,083
It's not a sudden blow either.
All that's for people with black money!

1316
01:30:29,167 --> 01:30:31,167
This is the biggest lottery
you've won in your life.

1317
01:30:33,458 --> 01:30:35,625
What are you saying? I don't understand.

1318
01:30:35,917 --> 01:30:38,625
This is the new 2000 rupees note
which is going to be released shortly.

1319
01:30:39,375 --> 01:30:41,792
A 2000 rupee note?
When did it come out?

1320
01:30:41,875 --> 01:30:44,125
Even the banks only start
to get them tomorrow.

1321
01:30:44,333 --> 01:30:47,833
Everyone thinks that a 1000 rupee note
is going to be released next.

1322
01:30:48,125 --> 01:30:51,333
But ten days after this,
it's a 500 rupee note that's coming out.

1323
01:30:52,667 --> 01:30:54,417
No one has seen that note's design,

1324
01:30:54,500 --> 01:30:57,750
except for some people at the reserve
bank and a few people like me.

1325
01:30:58,083 --> 01:31:00,708
By the time that note is released
and reaches the people,

1326
01:31:00,958 --> 01:31:04,167
you print the same note
and distribute it all over India!

1327
01:31:04,375 --> 01:31:06,625
By the time people recognize
which is original and which is fake,

1328
01:31:06,875 --> 01:31:09,417
at least ten billion fake currency
will be out in the market.

1329
01:31:09,542 --> 01:31:11,917
-Without a doubt!
-Yes!

1330
01:31:12,292 --> 01:31:14,083
Such a sharp mind! Great idea!

1331
01:31:14,542 --> 01:31:17,750
But how will I print a note
that no one has seen?

1332
01:31:17,833 --> 01:31:19,708
I will give you the design, man! Tomorrow.

1333
01:31:19,875 --> 01:31:21,917
I'm not playing from the supreme bank
for no reason.

1334
01:31:22,500 --> 01:31:25,458
Idea! Then what if we get
the original design for the 2000?

1335
01:31:25,583 --> 01:31:28,083
No! No! If you get over excited,
you'll be caught.

1336
01:31:28,292 --> 01:31:29,250
Five hundred is fine.

1337
01:31:29,375 --> 01:31:32,833
You will be the only fake note printer
in India who has the design of that note.

1338
01:31:40,667 --> 01:31:42,500
I don't need Indian money.
I can't trust it.

1339
01:31:42,625 --> 01:31:46,042
-Who knows when it'll get banned?
-The price is quite high.

1340
01:31:46,792 --> 01:31:47,792
But it's okay.

1341
01:31:48,542 --> 01:31:50,125
-Deal!
-That's it.

1342
01:31:57,708 --> 01:32:00,333
Twenty-seven-hundred-thousand

1343
01:32:00,458 --> 01:32:02,167
for that useless land?
Are you living in some other world?

1344
01:32:02,292 --> 01:32:03,958
It's because we need it urgently, Ikka.

1345
01:32:04,292 --> 01:32:06,667
When we went to the co-operative bank,
their state is worse than ours.

1346
01:32:06,875 --> 01:32:10,125
After this demonetization.
Please help us somehow.

1347
01:32:10,375 --> 01:32:13,333
Even if I decide to help, I have
only the old 500s and 1000s.

1348
01:32:13,875 --> 01:32:15,708
-Is that enough for you?
-What do I do with that?

1349
01:32:15,833 --> 01:32:17,958
If you want new notes,
you'll have to get it printed.

1350
01:32:18,250 --> 01:32:20,500
You go and bring the money
to get your documents back.

1351
01:32:20,667 --> 01:32:24,625
Or else you'll lose your house, Shaji!
I swear on Ikka. Right?

1352
01:32:26,083 --> 01:32:29,000
What is this? Then come and sit on my lap!
Come on!

1353
01:32:29,167 --> 01:32:30,167
Get out!

1354
01:32:30,250 --> 01:32:32,167
-What are you doing? Come here.
-So everything went well?

1355
01:32:32,292 --> 01:32:34,458
He has a good heart.
That's why he's in a wheelchair.

1356
01:32:41,083 --> 01:32:43,667
-Is it all true?
-Don't tempt me unnecessarily!

1357
01:32:43,958 --> 01:32:48,958
-Xavier, have I ever lied to you? Have I?
-No.

1358
01:32:49,708 --> 01:32:52,625
I will get the stuff by midnight tonight.

1359
01:32:53,042 --> 01:32:55,792
That's why I took a late flight
last night,

1360
01:32:56,000 --> 01:32:59,292
traveled four and a half hours by car
and came to this High Range.

1361
01:32:59,667 --> 01:33:03,833
What do I gain by helping Shettys
and Marwadis make money?

1362
01:33:04,333 --> 01:33:05,500
Tell me more.

1363
01:33:05,583 --> 01:33:09,042
I will send that thing
through two of my guys, tonight.

1364
01:33:09,167 --> 01:33:11,042
-On a local train.
-On a local train?

1365
01:33:11,125 --> 01:33:12,833
Yes. That is the safe route.

1366
01:33:13,750 --> 01:33:15,833
High tech smuggling can be tracked easily.

1367
01:33:16,042 --> 01:33:19,458
For deals like these, local set-ups are
better, so that no one suspects anything.

1368
01:33:19,917 --> 01:33:23,750
And which railway stations
don't have big crowds close by?

1369
01:33:23,958 --> 01:33:26,333
Gomangalam. It's a station
just for the sake of it.

1370
01:33:26,625 --> 01:33:30,250
-No one boards or gets off there.
-Both of you should be there.

1371
01:33:30,667 --> 01:33:35,792
Xavier, you shouldn't go. Just send them.
And... three million dollars.

1372
01:33:36,542 --> 01:33:38,125
That's the price of this mold.

1373
01:33:38,333 --> 01:33:40,750
You should send it with my guys
who are bringing the stuff.

1374
01:33:41,125 --> 01:33:43,708
Three million dollars.
A hundred and eighty million rupees?

1375
01:33:43,833 --> 01:33:46,042
-A hundred and eighty million rupees?
-Do you need it in dollars?

1376
01:33:46,292 --> 01:33:48,542
-Yes.
-So, cheers!

1377
01:33:53,792 --> 01:33:55,958
<i>A money mint worth millions and millions?</i>

1378
01:33:59,292 --> 01:34:02,750
<i>See. This is how the money mint mold</i>
<i>the new 500 rupees note,</i>

1379
01:34:02,875 --> 01:34:05,750
<i>which was meant for some fake currency</i>
<i>guy, Shetty, in Mangalore,</i>

1380
01:34:05,833 --> 01:34:07,333
<i>which set off to Gomangalam</i>
<i>for Satan Xavier,</i>

1381
01:34:07,417 --> 01:34:09,125
<i>after passing through many hands.</i>

1382
01:34:20,042 --> 01:34:24,125
-Lassar, sir. It's me. Shaji Pappan.
-What is it?

1383
01:34:24,250 --> 01:34:25,792
I need a little more time.

1384
01:34:25,917 --> 01:34:28,708
After this demonetization,
no one has any cash.

1385
01:34:30,917 --> 01:34:33,250
-Shajiyetta, he's not saying anything.
-He must be thinking.

1386
01:34:33,375 --> 01:34:36,542
Sachin is also like that. He'll make
a decision only after thinking twice.

1387
01:34:37,167 --> 01:34:39,833
Cry loudly! Let your Pappan hear you cry!

1388
01:34:41,125 --> 01:34:42,542
It's them!

1389
01:34:44,500 --> 01:34:48,875
Heard them, right? New notes.
Twenty-seven-hundred-thousand rupees

1390
01:34:49,333 --> 01:34:51,292
should be at Lassar's house
the day after tomorrow.

1391
01:34:56,792 --> 01:34:58,708
He's torturing my boys.

1392
01:35:07,417 --> 01:35:09,250
<i>Two parottas for both of you, right?</i>

1393
01:35:11,375 --> 01:35:13,833
Okay, Here you go. Hey, Sulaimaan!

1394
01:35:14,000 --> 01:35:15,208
Work faster!

1395
01:35:15,333 --> 01:35:17,750
-I'm doing it.
-There are many customers. Hurry up!

1396
01:35:18,917 --> 01:35:21,833
Didn't you find any other shop to eat at,
you scoundrels?

1397
01:35:22,125 --> 01:35:23,792
Look at him eating!

1398
01:35:25,792 --> 01:35:27,042
Dude, sir!

1399
01:35:29,542 --> 01:35:32,917
-You're in disguise?
-Hey, Soman!

1400
01:35:33,583 --> 01:35:35,750
-Are you doing good?
-Of course. I'm too good.

1401
01:35:35,875 --> 01:35:37,708
I'm in this position because of you!

1402
01:35:38,333 --> 01:35:40,167
-Where are the others?
-They are all here!

1403
01:35:40,292 --> 01:35:41,542
-Are they?
-Yes. Come!

1404
01:35:41,625 --> 01:35:43,000
-I've come with a new deal!
-Really?

1405
01:35:43,125 --> 01:35:45,208
I have an old deal to settle with you!

1406
01:35:45,500 --> 01:35:47,625
-I came at the right time then!
-I swear!

1407
01:35:47,792 --> 01:35:49,458
-Thank you!
-I looked for you everywhere!

1408
01:35:49,583 --> 01:35:51,250
Where are you going, Sulaimaan?

1409
01:35:51,375 --> 01:35:52,875
He's from my village, sir.

1410
01:35:52,958 --> 01:35:54,667
-Shall I serve an oothappam for Aunty?
-No.

1411
01:35:56,000 --> 01:35:59,875
<i>-What's that noise there?</i>
-Nothing, sir. It's a dog! A stray dog!

1412
01:36:00,375 --> 01:36:03,333
Tell them to stop, Dude.
Dragon, take them away!

1413
01:36:08,250 --> 01:36:09,917
New deal, Dude. Five billion!

1414
01:36:10,042 --> 01:36:12,000
Five billion!
Money mint! We can print!

1415
01:36:12,375 --> 01:36:14,167
-Five billion!
-Five billion?

1416
01:36:15,292 --> 01:36:17,833
-We can print. There's a money mint mold.
-He's correct.

1417
01:36:18,375 --> 01:36:19,708
Come on.

1418
01:36:24,208 --> 01:36:28,333
Money mint... Come on, boys! Follow me.

1419
01:36:29,542 --> 01:36:32,667
-Bro, are you hurt?
-This is nothing, man!

1420
01:36:33,500 --> 01:36:34,917
Wasn't he just beaten up?

1421
01:36:59,917 --> 01:37:00,917
Sulaimaan?

1422
01:37:11,250 --> 01:37:13,917
-What is this, Sulaimaan?
-Not Sulaimaan.

1423
01:37:14,042 --> 01:37:17,042
Damodaran Unni's son, Dilman Edakkochi.

1424
01:37:19,792 --> 01:37:21,583
People call me... Dude.

1425
01:37:43,917 --> 01:37:46,083
Oops. I forgot something!

1426
01:37:49,000 --> 01:37:50,000
Got it!

1427
01:38:16,958 --> 01:38:18,333
Hey, Maan!

1428
01:38:19,875 --> 01:38:21,708
I will not spare you!

1429
01:38:22,792 --> 01:38:25,583
Dude, sir, so you remember
whatever I told you, right?

1430
01:38:25,708 --> 01:38:27,750
I will stop the car
on top of Mookkumkuthi bridge.

1431
01:38:27,917 --> 01:38:29,750
Then I will lift the bonnet.
That's the signal.

1432
01:38:30,667 --> 01:38:32,875
Don't create a ruckus there
by firing and shooting!

1433
01:38:33,125 --> 01:38:36,458
That won't be necessary.
This is not like the old herb deal.

1434
01:38:38,000 --> 01:38:40,583
These fools won't be alone.
I'll be dealing directly.

1435
01:38:41,292 --> 01:38:42,333
That's better.

1436
01:38:42,583 --> 01:38:45,208
Shall I go then? Or else Satan Xavier
will suspect me!

1437
01:38:45,375 --> 01:38:47,792
And half the notes you print
would be for me, right?

1438
01:38:48,583 --> 01:38:49,583
No, right?

1439
01:38:51,333 --> 01:38:52,958
I asked you to wash the van, you fool!

1440
01:38:53,042 --> 01:38:54,542
It's been a long time since you
had a wash, right?

1441
01:38:55,083 --> 01:38:56,750
-Hey.
-What is it, Shajiyetta?

1442
01:38:57,958 --> 01:38:59,042
I was thinking,

1443
01:38:59,583 --> 01:39:02,625
-shall we all go together to their place?
-And then?

1444
01:39:03,250 --> 01:39:05,000
Then what? We'll start!

1445
01:39:05,500 --> 01:39:07,083
And then we'll escape.
What else is there to do?

1446
01:39:07,167 --> 01:39:08,750
With this back pain? Pappan?

1447
01:39:08,875 --> 01:39:11,125
-Best!
-We should bring our boys back, right?

1448
01:39:11,542 --> 01:39:14,125
You saw that Lassar, right?
He's as big as a baby elephant.

1449
01:39:14,333 --> 01:39:16,542
He won't fall even if we hit him
with a shovel.

1450
01:39:16,833 --> 01:39:18,208
Pull off some trick, Pappan!

1451
01:39:20,417 --> 01:39:23,083
Cleetus, how much will we get
if we sell your necklace?

1452
01:39:23,958 --> 01:39:25,875
If we sell this, around ten...

1453
01:39:26,167 --> 01:39:28,250
-That would be enough, right?
-...around 350 rupees.

1454
01:39:28,625 --> 01:39:29,958
But will they buy rolled gold?

1455
01:39:30,083 --> 01:39:31,917
-What is he saying?
-Get lost!

1456
01:39:33,458 --> 01:39:34,708
Hello, brother!

1457
01:39:36,250 --> 01:39:37,667
-How are you?
-Cleetus!

1458
01:39:37,792 --> 01:39:38,792
Good! Good!

1459
01:39:39,375 --> 01:39:41,625
-Abu?
-Give it to me.

1460
01:39:43,375 --> 01:39:44,917
Hello, it's Arakkal Abu.

1461
01:39:45,292 --> 01:39:48,292
Hello, Brother Abu. We'll reach
Gomangalam station at 11 a.m.

1462
01:39:49,083 --> 01:39:50,542
<i>Go there directly with the money.</i>

1463
01:39:50,917 --> 01:39:54,250
We don't have the time to get off there.
We're going directly to Palakkad.

1464
01:39:54,417 --> 01:39:58,042
-Okay.
-And one more thing. We need new notes.

1465
01:39:58,208 --> 01:40:00,833
If you don't have new notes,
even 50s and 100s will be fine.

1466
01:40:01,208 --> 01:40:03,000
But we don't need the old currency.

1467
01:40:03,125 --> 01:40:05,500
We are-- Will be there--
To get the stuff.

1468
01:40:07,833 --> 01:40:10,417
Shajiyetta, that was the Bengali
with the medicine.

1469
01:40:10,625 --> 01:40:12,833
They will reach Gomangalam
station tomorrow at 11 a.m.

1470
01:40:13,583 --> 01:40:16,833
-Medicine in between all this?
-My dear Shajiyetta, please buy it!

1471
01:40:17,250 --> 01:40:18,208
And, yeah, Shajiyetta,

1472
01:40:18,375 --> 01:40:20,958
even these Bengalis know
about the demonetization now.

1473
01:40:21,292 --> 01:40:24,000
But how do we manage
the 15,000 to give them?

1474
01:40:24,167 --> 01:40:27,625
I am very sure that with this medicine,
Pappan's back pain would be cured.

1475
01:40:27,917 --> 01:40:30,167
If Pappan's back pain is cured
with that medicine,

1476
01:40:30,292 --> 01:40:32,958
-we can go thrash them to pulp, right?
-Yes!

1477
01:40:33,583 --> 01:40:35,375
I don't have the money
for the medicine, man!

1478
01:40:35,583 --> 01:40:37,625
Think about how we're going to get
our boys back.

1479
01:40:39,250 --> 01:40:41,458
-Pappan!
-What is it?

1480
01:40:41,625 --> 01:40:43,833
Mom went on a visit to the ICU
and hasn't left!

1481
01:40:43,958 --> 01:40:45,000
Is that her new home?

1482
01:40:45,125 --> 01:40:47,708
She swore that she won't come back
unless you return the documents.

1483
01:40:47,833 --> 01:40:49,083
-I'm very happy!
-And then,

1484
01:40:49,792 --> 01:40:53,167
this has all the money I made
by selling goat milk and the big goat.

1485
01:40:53,708 --> 01:40:56,417
It's all in change.
I saved it to buy a scooter.

1486
01:40:57,042 --> 01:40:59,417
Anyway, it would be more than 15,000.

1487
01:40:59,583 --> 01:41:01,292
-Here you go, Pappan.
-Take it, Pappan.

1488
01:41:01,708 --> 01:41:03,042
Take it, Shajiyetta.

1489
01:41:03,958 --> 01:41:06,000
Get your back pain sorted
and thrash them, Pappan!

1490
01:41:06,208 --> 01:41:08,000
That's it!

1491
01:41:27,958 --> 01:41:30,917
So you remember everything, right?
Everything should be as per the plan!

1492
01:41:31,083 --> 01:41:32,583
There are three million dollars in this.

1493
01:41:32,708 --> 01:41:35,708
Go straight to Gomangalam station.
Only they will be there.

1494
01:41:36,458 --> 01:41:38,792
Pay the money, and buy the money mint.

1495
01:41:38,917 --> 01:41:41,167
And you'll reach the place I told you
without anyone noticing.

1496
01:41:41,333 --> 01:41:42,458
-Okay, sir.
-Okay?

1497
01:41:45,875 --> 01:41:49,208
-Just a minute. Paying, getting. Simple.
-Go! Go! Go!

1498
01:41:51,542 --> 01:41:55,292
-How is my tie, Soman?
-Aren't you ashamed to wear it?

1499
01:41:55,458 --> 01:41:57,083
We're going for such a big deal, right?

1500
01:41:57,208 --> 01:42:00,125
They should understand
that we're not ordinary people.

1501
01:42:16,083 --> 01:42:18,958
-What was the name of that station?
-Gomangalam.

1502
01:42:24,083 --> 01:42:27,458
-What kind of a station is this?
-What is this? Legislative assembly?

1503
01:42:28,083 --> 01:42:30,917
Hey! Hold this. It's too heavy.

1504
01:42:31,083 --> 01:42:33,500
With all the change and chips,
why not add a couple of jackfruits?

1505
01:42:33,667 --> 01:42:35,708
Will they bring the medicine unharmed?

1506
01:42:44,417 --> 01:42:47,250
-Stop! Stop!
-I am stopping.

1507
01:42:48,708 --> 01:42:51,000
Isn't that Sarbath Shemeer?

1508
01:42:51,083 --> 01:42:52,625
Why is he at this station?

1509
01:42:52,792 --> 01:42:55,500
-The train is about to reach--
-Hands up!

1510
01:42:57,917 --> 01:42:59,875
Slowly. Bend down and go.

1511
01:43:02,125 --> 01:43:04,792
<i>When I reach the station</i>
<i>after sending them in the Madurai train,</i>

1512
01:43:04,917 --> 01:43:06,375
<i>the case file should be on my table.</i>

1513
01:43:06,458 --> 01:43:08,542
Hey! Don't say that we hit you
when lawyers ask you.

1514
01:43:08,667 --> 01:43:10,417
-Come!
-Sarbath. I need a salted soda.

1515
01:43:10,542 --> 01:43:12,292
I'll try telling him.
It's Sarbath Shemeer.

1516
01:43:13,208 --> 01:43:15,417
-Pappan!
-Why are you getting scared?

1517
01:43:15,583 --> 01:43:17,625
-We are the police, right?
-Correct.

1518
01:43:17,917 --> 01:43:19,542
I'll scare them. What are you doing here?

1519
01:43:19,625 --> 01:43:21,583
Did you come to plant a bomb
in a deserted station?

1520
01:43:21,708 --> 01:43:24,375
No, sir. I came to buy medicine
for my back pain.

1521
01:43:24,500 --> 01:43:26,875
Don't lie. Is your dad running
a medical store here?

1522
01:43:27,000 --> 01:43:29,167
-No, sir. It's coming from abroad.
-Abroad?

1523
01:43:29,292 --> 01:43:31,583
Yeah. From Rajasthan.
They will bring it on the train now.

1524
01:43:32,958 --> 01:43:36,000
Remember one thing.
I will always have an eye on you!

1525
01:43:36,125 --> 01:43:37,208
-As you say, sir.
-Sir,

1526
01:43:37,375 --> 01:43:39,417
is it true that you don't know
how to salute?

1527
01:43:40,167 --> 01:43:41,917
Sir, show him how it's done.

1528
01:43:43,417 --> 01:43:44,417
Give it.

1529
01:43:46,875 --> 01:43:49,750
-It's correct.
-That was awesome.

1530
01:43:51,083 --> 01:43:53,458
That is how you make a policeman
salute you!

1531
01:43:54,958 --> 01:43:58,792
-His respect for me has increased, right?
-I felt that they were mocking you, sir.

1532
01:43:58,917 --> 01:44:01,417
-No. He's more respectful now.
-Then it must be right.

1533
01:44:01,583 --> 01:44:03,917
Sir, he's out of the district.
Shall we catch him now?

1534
01:44:04,042 --> 01:44:07,542
You fool! He didn't leave the district.
He only left the state, right?

1535
01:44:08,500 --> 01:44:11,542
Then where is this district?
What is that for, sir?

1536
01:44:12,667 --> 01:44:14,917
Who knows when we're going to see
these guys again!

1537
01:44:16,125 --> 01:44:18,417
But this district and state...

1538
01:44:19,333 --> 01:44:22,125
-Jesus! Shaji Pappan!
-Did they ban the train along with notes?

1539
01:44:22,208 --> 01:44:26,125
Whenever I see him, I get caught
by the police. Today as well. Come!

1540
01:44:26,583 --> 01:44:27,792
Come!

1541
01:44:32,917 --> 01:44:35,833
Hey, brother. Wake up.
We've reached the station.

1542
01:44:36,083 --> 01:44:37,083
Come on!

1543
01:44:48,750 --> 01:44:53,042
-How do we find them?
-Medicine guy? Medicine guy?

1544
01:44:53,292 --> 01:44:55,167
Shajiyetta, they will only understand
if we call in Hindi.

1545
01:44:55,250 --> 01:44:58,667
-Then you call.
-Brother Medicine!

1546
01:44:58,792 --> 01:45:01,958
Here he is. There are two of them?
Is this the stuff?

1547
01:45:02,917 --> 01:45:06,292
-Police?
-Police are our friends! But Fakru?

1548
01:45:06,417 --> 01:45:08,375
Isn't this Fakru?
Didn't you see the box?

1549
01:45:08,500 --> 01:45:12,042
Isn't this the medicine, for the back?
Here! Hold the money!

1550
01:45:12,458 --> 01:45:13,875
My back pain!

1551
01:45:15,083 --> 01:45:17,583
-Sir, selfie?
-Okay!

1552
01:45:23,958 --> 01:45:25,250
Okay, then.

1553
01:45:27,083 --> 01:45:29,000
He doesn't hug his own dad like that.

1554
01:45:30,042 --> 01:45:31,625
Bye!

1555
01:45:36,750 --> 01:45:39,167
Pappan! Come here.

1556
01:45:39,500 --> 01:45:41,708
Get back to the district
before dark, before I notice.

1557
01:45:41,792 --> 01:45:43,625
And no one should know that we met here.

1558
01:45:43,833 --> 01:45:44,833
Medicine?

1559
01:45:44,958 --> 01:45:47,458
-Hey! Which Indian state was it?
-Bengal.

1560
01:45:47,583 --> 01:45:50,125
-That's what I studied somewhere.
-Pappan!

1561
01:45:51,083 --> 01:45:53,042
I hope I'm cured at least with this, boys.

1562
01:45:53,167 --> 01:45:54,458
You will be okay, Pappan!

1563
01:45:59,083 --> 01:46:02,042
Gomangalam? Hey!

1564
01:46:02,167 --> 01:46:03,750
-We reached Gomangalam station.
-What happened?

1565
01:46:04,125 --> 01:46:07,583
We have to get off. Take the stuff.
Hey! Stop the train!

1566
01:46:08,708 --> 01:46:12,333
-Come on!
-At least don't lose this one, Cleetus.

1567
01:46:13,000 --> 01:46:15,333
Idiots. They didn't see us.
Both Pappan and the train left.

1568
01:46:15,417 --> 01:46:18,417
-The train also left.
-Both Pappan and the train left.

1569
01:46:18,500 --> 01:46:19,708
Hey! Come!

1570
01:46:22,917 --> 01:46:26,000
God! Did everyone leave?
There's no one here.

1571
01:46:26,125 --> 01:46:27,667
What do we tell Satan now?

1572
01:46:27,750 --> 01:46:30,500
-We'll have to hear all his cusses!
-Soman! No one has gone.

1573
01:46:30,667 --> 01:46:32,917
-They got here okay.
-Why didn't you tell me earlier?

1574
01:46:33,083 --> 01:46:35,167
-Come fast. Don't lose our standard.
-No way.

1575
01:46:35,833 --> 01:46:37,708
Look at them standing
with the currency mold.

1576
01:46:37,833 --> 01:46:40,042
-Yes. Looks like Beemappalli.
-Namaste.

1577
01:46:40,208 --> 01:46:44,167
We were hiding because the police
were here.

1578
01:46:44,375 --> 01:46:45,458
Who are you both?

1579
01:46:45,583 --> 01:46:47,458
-What?
-Where is Abu and Cleetus?

1580
01:46:47,958 --> 01:46:49,875
Where are those sons of Satan?

1581
01:46:51,000 --> 01:46:53,250
Hey, brother! We are the sons of Satan.

1582
01:46:53,417 --> 01:46:55,500
Can't you guess by how we look?
We are his boys!

1583
01:46:55,708 --> 01:46:56,875
-Hold this.
-What is this?

1584
01:46:56,958 --> 01:46:57,958
-It's a box.
-Give it here.

1585
01:46:58,625 --> 01:47:00,958
Listen. There's one thing.

1586
01:47:01,208 --> 01:47:04,458
Drink it mixed with cow urine
every morning.

1587
01:47:04,833 --> 01:47:05,708
What?

1588
01:47:05,792 --> 01:47:07,375
He says that you'll have to drink
cow urine.

1589
01:47:07,500 --> 01:47:10,500
-I won't drink.
-I'll drink it. You get the box.

1590
01:47:10,833 --> 01:47:12,792
Only you North Indians need
to drink cow urine!

1591
01:47:13,042 --> 01:47:15,792
-What is he saying?
-Who are these people?

1592
01:47:15,958 --> 01:47:18,958
-Why didn't Abu and Cleetus come?
-They must have had some other work.

1593
01:47:19,167 --> 01:47:21,167
But they sent the right people.

1594
01:47:21,583 --> 01:47:23,875
-But...
-What do you want, brother?

1595
01:47:23,958 --> 01:47:25,625
-Money!
-Money is in there, right?

1596
01:47:25,833 --> 01:47:28,167
Fifteen thousand rupees in such a big bag?

1597
01:47:28,542 --> 01:47:30,875
There will be Kerala chips in it, brother.

1598
01:47:33,333 --> 01:47:37,042
Hey, Soman. When they said
it's a money mint, I thought

1599
01:47:37,167 --> 01:47:40,083
it would look like a big can
which can hold up to ten liters of arrack.

1600
01:47:40,250 --> 01:47:41,917
But this... Nice!

1601
01:47:42,625 --> 01:47:45,208
This is not a mint, man.
It's a design to print notes.

1602
01:47:45,333 --> 01:47:47,042
People simply call it a money mint.

1603
01:47:51,083 --> 01:47:52,083
What happened?

1604
01:47:52,458 --> 01:47:54,042
There's something wrong with it
at times.

1605
01:47:54,125 --> 01:47:56,000
Yeah. Might be out of Diesel. Check!

1606
01:47:56,417 --> 01:47:59,250
Didn't I ask them to wait here?

1607
01:47:59,458 --> 01:48:01,167
There wasn't any problem when I drove.

1608
01:48:03,125 --> 01:48:05,208
Where the hell are they?

1609
01:48:05,833 --> 01:48:08,083
-Hey!
-Okay, right?

1610
01:48:12,083 --> 01:48:16,042
Hey, blackie with the box!
Come here. Come here.

1611
01:48:17,583 --> 01:48:19,250
-Gun?
-Come here.

1612
01:48:19,500 --> 01:48:21,583
I won't give you this.
This belongs to Satan, sir.

1613
01:48:23,750 --> 01:48:25,417
-Come here.
-Don't shoot here.

1614
01:48:26,292 --> 01:48:30,500
It's some big team. Give them the stuff.
Come! Come out.

1615
01:48:31,000 --> 01:48:32,292
-Come!
-Should I?

1616
01:48:32,375 --> 01:48:34,625
-Come here! Fast!
-Or they'll kill us! Give it!

1617
01:48:34,875 --> 01:48:37,833
-We needn't be shot dead, right?
-Say sorry.

1618
01:48:41,250 --> 01:48:43,542
We got it with so much difficulty, sir.

1619
01:48:45,042 --> 01:48:46,833
-Give it.
-Give me the box, you black bear!

1620
01:48:47,083 --> 01:48:49,375
-Give it. He's pointing the gun.
-Get lost. I won't give it.

1621
01:48:50,333 --> 01:48:52,583
You need honesty towards your job!

1622
01:48:55,333 --> 01:48:57,333
-What is this?
-Earthquake?

1623
01:48:58,708 --> 01:49:01,583
-What's happening?
-Hey!

1624
01:49:02,542 --> 01:49:04,625
-Wasn't that a gunshot?
-Yes.

1625
01:49:04,792 --> 01:49:06,958
-Let's clear out.
-Hurry up.

1626
01:49:07,042 --> 01:49:08,458
-Go fast.
-Yes.

1627
01:49:08,625 --> 01:49:09,750
-Go fast!
-No!

1628
01:49:12,542 --> 01:49:14,042
-This is vehicle, Dude.
-Stop the vehicle!

1629
01:49:14,583 --> 01:49:15,458
Reach for it, Dude.

1630
01:49:15,750 --> 01:49:18,417
No! My box! Give it, you dog!

1631
01:49:18,833 --> 01:49:20,833
Get lost, you dog! This is our box!

1632
01:49:20,917 --> 01:49:23,708
You're lucky that my muscles
sprained when you pointed the gun!

1633
01:49:24,542 --> 01:49:27,125
You asked me to hide on top of a lorry?
You dog!

1634
01:49:27,750 --> 01:49:31,000
Didn't I tell you not to wear
sunglasses?

1635
01:49:31,333 --> 01:49:33,167
All you idiots are blind!

1636
01:49:36,542 --> 01:49:38,292
Boss! Success!

1637
01:49:40,042 --> 01:49:41,542
-Check it out.
-But, Xavier, sir,

1638
01:49:41,667 --> 01:49:43,792
I don't understand who tried to steal
our money mint

1639
01:49:43,917 --> 01:49:46,083
at gunpoint on the way!

1640
01:49:46,250 --> 01:49:47,792
-Even me.
-Enemies are everywhere.

1641
01:49:47,875 --> 01:49:48,833
Was it them?

1642
01:49:48,958 --> 01:49:51,708
Idiots! They must have reached
Coimbatore in that lorry.

1643
01:49:52,917 --> 01:49:55,375
-We got our money mint, right?
-Yes!

1644
01:50:00,625 --> 01:50:03,625
What is this, Soman?
Your dad's street medicine shop?

1645
01:50:04,042 --> 01:50:06,125
Check properly, sir.
It must be in that bottle.

1646
01:50:07,667 --> 01:50:11,500
-God! I hope this is it.
-"Daily, three times...

1647
01:50:12,125 --> 01:50:14,500
Apply it three times a day before a bath.

1648
01:50:14,708 --> 01:50:18,417
-Your pain will be cured." What is this?
-This is what they gave us.

1649
01:50:22,208 --> 01:50:24,167
Where is my money mint?

1650
01:50:29,500 --> 01:50:30,875
What is this?

1651
01:50:33,708 --> 01:50:36,125
-Shajiyetta!
-Bring it here, man!

1652
01:50:38,417 --> 01:50:39,708
Shajiyetta, look at this.

1653
01:50:39,875 --> 01:50:42,333
-No need to look. Just apply it.
-No, Shajiyetta. Look at this!

1654
01:50:42,500 --> 01:50:44,083
This was inside the box!

1655
01:50:45,125 --> 01:50:46,458
What is this?

1656
01:50:48,583 --> 01:50:49,583
Is it tasty?

1657
01:50:50,958 --> 01:50:52,250
Is it a metal?

1658
01:50:52,833 --> 01:50:55,458
Should we apply it on the back
after grinding all of it together?

1659
01:50:55,542 --> 01:50:58,250
No, Shajiyetta. It looks like
some antique. Look at this.

1660
01:50:58,417 --> 01:50:59,750
There's a photo of some king.

1661
01:51:00,750 --> 01:51:02,000
Hey! It's not that!

1662
01:51:02,458 --> 01:51:04,500
I think this is the photo
of the physician who made this.

1663
01:51:05,208 --> 01:51:08,000
Pappan, it has 500 written on it.
It must be 500 years old.

1664
01:51:08,208 --> 01:51:10,417
-Will it be the physician's number?
-Shall we call them?

1665
01:51:10,583 --> 01:51:13,208
You guys are such fools!
There are many pieces, right?

1666
01:51:13,417 --> 01:51:16,167
We should put all of them together,
keep it on Pappan's back and weld it.

1667
01:51:16,292 --> 01:51:17,542
Then weld it on my chest!

1668
01:51:17,708 --> 01:51:20,042
Shajiyetta, I can't reach that Fakru
on his phone.

1669
01:51:20,167 --> 01:51:21,167
You won't!

1670
01:51:21,292 --> 01:51:24,292
Are all of you happy now that we've lost
that poor Rachel's 15,000 rupees?

1671
01:51:24,417 --> 01:51:25,417
Scumbags!

1672
01:51:26,833 --> 01:51:27,917
-Pappan!
-Go to hell!

1673
01:51:28,000 --> 01:51:31,000
-Shajiyetta, what do we do now?
-Give it to some scrap dealer.

1674
01:51:31,083 --> 01:51:32,750
Then shall we give it to Iron Abdullah?

1675
01:51:33,208 --> 01:51:35,667
His back ache has become
a headache for us.

1676
01:51:35,792 --> 01:51:36,833
Get in fast.

1677
01:51:39,083 --> 01:51:40,083
Xavier, sir...

1678
01:51:41,000 --> 01:51:44,000
I am sure those tug of war idiots
will have the stuff.

1679
01:51:44,333 --> 01:51:46,583
There was no one else at the station
apart from them.

1680
01:51:46,750 --> 01:51:47,875
-Isn't that so?
-Is it?

1681
01:51:49,708 --> 01:51:52,167
-Where would they be?
-They will be at home.

1682
01:51:52,375 --> 01:51:53,625
Where else would they go?

1683
01:51:53,958 --> 01:51:56,375
Shall we go to his house and kidnap
that Pappan's mom?

1684
01:51:57,083 --> 01:52:00,042
-Good idea!
-What did you say?

1685
01:52:00,458 --> 01:52:04,375
-We'll kidnap his mom!
-Or no need. Dad, mom or sister?

1686
01:52:04,500 --> 01:52:06,333
Then that hag will be my responsibility!

1687
01:52:06,625 --> 01:52:10,583
Xavier, sir, that is Pappan's niece.

1688
01:52:11,042 --> 01:52:15,250
-Shall we kidnap her instead of his mom?
-That's correct, Xavier, sir.

1689
01:52:15,708 --> 01:52:19,917
If we kidnap the girl, whoever it is,
they will come to us like dogs,

1690
01:52:20,042 --> 01:52:22,000
scared of shame. What do you say?

1691
01:52:24,292 --> 01:52:27,375
This is the first time in my life
I've done such a cheap thing.

1692
01:52:28,208 --> 01:52:31,125
I don't have time. That's the only reason
I'm doing this.

1693
01:52:32,292 --> 01:52:35,125
You guys, go and kidnap her.

1694
01:52:36,167 --> 01:52:40,042
Done. Soman, show some fury!

1695
01:52:40,625 --> 01:52:42,833
She'll know what the power
of this battery is.

1696
01:52:44,375 --> 01:52:46,875
Hey, girl! Don't make too much noise.

1697
01:52:47,208 --> 01:52:50,458
You better come and get into that Jeep.
Rest, we'll talk after that.

1698
01:52:50,917 --> 01:52:52,542
-Go!
-Didn't you hear him?

1699
01:52:52,917 --> 01:52:56,417
It's Satan Xavier in that Jeep.
However much you shout, we'll take you.

1700
01:52:57,458 --> 01:52:59,750
-That will be a disgrace for you.
-What say you then?

1701
01:53:00,250 --> 01:53:02,750
Will you get in yourself,
or should we carry you?

1702
01:53:07,042 --> 01:53:07,917
What?

1703
01:53:14,083 --> 01:53:16,750
KATTAPPANA ACADEMY OF SHOTOKAN
KARATE AND SHAOLIN KUNG FU

1704
01:53:33,375 --> 01:53:36,708
-Soman, don't get up!
-She'll kick you if you get up.

1705
01:53:37,292 --> 01:53:40,625
Boss, start the car!
She's from a badass family.

1706
01:53:47,500 --> 01:53:49,208
This thing...

1707
01:53:54,750 --> 01:54:00,333
I think these are the duplicates of coins
used by Sultans who ruled 500 years back.

1708
01:54:00,792 --> 01:54:04,625
Anyway it's written 500. So I'll add
another zero and give you 5,000.

1709
01:54:04,792 --> 01:54:07,708
Five thousand won't be enough.
We bought it with a lot of money.

1710
01:54:07,833 --> 01:54:08,792
Let's do one thing.

1711
01:54:08,958 --> 01:54:11,208
-I'm not selling it. I'll keep it at home.
-Don't say that.

1712
01:54:11,500 --> 01:54:13,583
Anyway, you guys came
all the way here, right?

1713
01:54:13,708 --> 01:54:15,333
Don't make it in vain. Quote a price.

1714
01:54:16,583 --> 01:54:21,125
-The price would be... 16,000...
-One hundred thousand.

1715
01:54:22,583 --> 01:54:23,458
Yes.

1716
01:54:23,833 --> 01:54:26,542
One hundred thousand is too much.
That won't be possible.

1717
01:54:26,833 --> 01:54:28,042
What do I say?

1718
01:54:28,167 --> 01:54:31,708
I love these old things like antiques
a little too much.

1719
01:54:31,833 --> 01:54:34,292
Whatever! I'll add another zero
and give you 50,000.

1720
01:54:34,375 --> 01:54:35,250
That's fair.

1721
01:54:35,625 --> 01:54:37,833
-Then add two, three more zeroes, please.
-Yes.

1722
01:54:38,125 --> 01:54:40,792
Right from childhood, Shajiyettan
has been deeply in love with zeroes.

1723
01:54:40,958 --> 01:54:41,917
Really? Why not?

1724
01:54:42,042 --> 01:54:44,250
There are already three to four zeroes
in 50,000.

1725
01:54:44,708 --> 01:54:47,750
-Fifty thousand?
-It's okay, right?

1726
01:54:48,083 --> 01:54:50,708
-Definitely.
-Here you go.

1727
01:54:52,875 --> 01:54:54,417
Not 1,000 or 500. Okay then.

1728
01:54:55,083 --> 01:54:58,042
Come. There's relaxation
after demonetization now.

1729
01:54:58,250 --> 01:55:00,958
-What do we do for the rest of the money?
-We can sell Pappan's kidney for that.

1730
01:55:01,083 --> 01:55:02,458
-What?
-We can sell his kidney.

1731
01:55:02,583 --> 01:55:03,917
Mine? I sold that long back.

1732
01:55:04,000 --> 01:55:08,000
Hey! Why did he pay 50,000
for this thing worth 15,000?

1733
01:55:08,292 --> 01:55:10,500
What if it's not an antique?
What if it's gold? Shall we check?

1734
01:55:10,583 --> 01:55:13,208
Shajiyetta! It's an antique. I am sure.

1735
01:55:13,375 --> 01:55:14,667
I've dealt with a lot of antiques.

1736
01:55:14,792 --> 01:55:16,833
Just think that we fooled him
and made some money.

1737
01:55:16,958 --> 01:55:20,000
Hey! Isn't Pappan's van
older than that antique?

1738
01:55:20,708 --> 01:55:22,625
-What will we get if we sell this?
-A kick from me!

1739
01:55:22,750 --> 01:55:24,042
Come! Let's try to get our boys out.

1740
01:55:24,167 --> 01:55:25,542
-What is this, man?
-Come!

1741
01:55:29,917 --> 01:55:30,917
Lonappan!

1742
01:55:31,750 --> 01:55:34,250
Once they leave,
get our special vehicle out.

1743
01:55:34,625 --> 01:55:36,917
We need to rush to Coimbatore.

1744
01:55:37,667 --> 01:55:39,583
-Okay, Ikka.
-Oh, God!

1745
01:55:39,833 --> 01:55:43,083
This Abdullah thought everything
was over with the demonetization!

1746
01:55:43,292 --> 01:55:47,500
God! You're showering this poor
smuggler with blessings again and again!

1747
01:55:47,583 --> 01:55:48,833
Oh, God!

1748
01:56:14,333 --> 01:56:16,542
-You don't have much discipline.
-I also felt so, sir.

1749
01:56:17,667 --> 01:56:19,208
You learned a lot
of things today.

1750
01:56:19,333 --> 01:56:21,125
If you pay attention,
I'll make you another Shemeer.

1751
01:56:21,250 --> 01:56:22,833
-Come on!
-Will I be such a disaster?

1752
01:56:25,208 --> 01:56:26,917
Aashaan has sent me a
message on WhatsApp.

1753
01:56:27,042 --> 01:56:28,708
Will it be your suspension letter?

1754
01:56:30,458 --> 01:56:32,875
Aashaan is always observing me.

1755
01:56:33,625 --> 01:56:34,625
My time has changed.

1756
01:56:34,708 --> 01:56:37,958
That's why I felt like posing
for this photo even though I barged in!

1757
01:56:38,083 --> 01:56:40,250
Now I'll only have success.
Aashaan is calling.

1758
01:56:41,708 --> 01:56:43,958
-You have forgiven me?
-Like hell!

1759
01:56:44,375 --> 01:56:46,167
-Where's that Kammatipadam?
-Kammatipadam?

1760
01:56:46,500 --> 01:56:50,875
In the photo I sent now, you're all active
while that Kammatipadam was exchanged.

1761
01:56:51,333 --> 01:56:53,375
The Central Intelligence
Department sent me that photo.

1762
01:56:53,583 --> 01:56:55,833
-Sir, I--
-Don't speak a word!

1763
01:56:56,000 --> 01:56:57,333
<i>A team has set off from there.</i>

1764
01:56:57,792 --> 01:57:01,000
If you don't catch the people
who smuggled it this evening,

1765
01:57:01,167 --> 01:57:02,667
you're gone!

1766
01:57:03,000 --> 01:57:06,333
Are you complying with insurgents now,
you rascal?

1767
01:57:08,167 --> 01:57:10,708
-What is this Kammatipadam?
-Isn't that Dulquer Salmaan's movie?

1768
01:57:10,833 --> 01:57:13,042
-How can that be carried in a box?
-Which box?

1769
01:57:13,208 --> 01:57:16,208
-This box with this bloody Pappan.
-That must be the film box.

1770
01:57:19,875 --> 01:57:21,250
Shajiyetta, phone for you.

1771
01:57:21,458 --> 01:57:23,875
Jesus! It must be from the hospital
to pay the bill.

1772
01:57:24,667 --> 01:57:26,750
-Hello!
-You bloody insurgent, Pappan!

1773
01:57:26,875 --> 01:57:28,875
Have you turned into an
international underworld criminal now?

1774
01:57:29,083 --> 01:57:32,250
I don't have anything to do with Lassar.
When they caught my boys--

1775
01:57:32,333 --> 01:57:34,167
If they catch your boys,
will you print fake notes?

1776
01:57:34,458 --> 01:57:35,958
When no one
has any notes with them too!

1777
01:57:38,708 --> 01:57:41,875
-Fake notes?
-You better stay where you are.

1778
01:57:42,083 --> 01:57:44,333
And when I come,
that Kammatipadam-- Sheesh!

1779
01:57:44,500 --> 01:57:45,708
Surrender with that Kammatam.

1780
01:57:47,292 --> 01:57:51,167
Hey! We bought a money mint instead
of the medicine at the railway station!

1781
01:57:51,500 --> 01:57:53,542
Hello! He switched off his phone.

1782
01:57:54,042 --> 01:57:55,625
-Govindan, park the car there.
-Sir.

1783
01:57:55,917 --> 01:58:00,417
Shajiyetta, we have unknowingly
turned into underworld criminals already!

1784
01:58:00,542 --> 01:58:02,000
You and your underworld!

1785
01:58:03,500 --> 01:58:05,542
-Why are you crying like that?
-It's my phone.

1786
01:58:06,208 --> 01:58:07,625
I just got a message.

1787
01:58:08,125 --> 01:58:09,625
-God! What's the next trouble--
-Shajiyetta!

1788
01:58:09,917 --> 01:58:12,208
-It's us!
-Us?

1789
01:58:15,625 --> 01:58:17,708
God! Why does it say insurgents and all?

1790
01:58:19,417 --> 01:58:23,750
-Pappan, did we become famous so quickly?
-Jesus! I think the police will catch us.

1791
01:58:23,875 --> 01:58:24,958
Start the car, Pappan!

1792
01:58:25,292 --> 01:58:28,500
He fooled us by only giving us 50,000.
We should get the mint back from him!

1793
01:58:30,000 --> 01:58:32,208
You have dealt with a lot of antiques,
right?

1794
01:58:32,583 --> 01:58:35,042
I've bought so many appams
and curries for you, right?

1795
01:58:35,708 --> 01:58:37,208
I hope he is still there.

1796
01:58:40,875 --> 01:58:43,125
<i>The intelligence report</i>
<i>says that the design</i>

1797
01:58:43,208 --> 01:58:45,292
<i>of the new 500-rupee notes</i>
<i>has been leaked...</i>

1798
01:58:45,792 --> 01:58:48,292
These guys used to play
around in our neighborhood, right?

1799
01:58:48,417 --> 01:58:49,417
Yes!

1800
01:58:49,542 --> 01:58:52,708
Within the blink of an eye,
they became insurgents!

1801
01:58:53,417 --> 01:58:54,542
What progress!

1802
01:58:54,750 --> 01:58:56,958
<i>Intelligence sent out the photo</i>
<i>of the exchange...</i>

1803
01:58:58,125 --> 01:58:59,667
Isn't that our Shaji Pappan?

1804
01:59:02,500 --> 01:59:05,417
<i>Opposition demanded that the insurgents</i>
<i>should be arrested immediately,</i>

1805
01:59:05,542 --> 01:59:08,583
<i>and the home minister should accept</i>
<i>responsibility and resign soon!</i>

1806
01:59:09,625 --> 01:59:12,542
Lonappan, switch on that light
and speed up!

1807
01:59:12,667 --> 01:59:14,625
-Then no one will suspect us.
-Okay.

1808
01:59:18,333 --> 01:59:20,333
Couldn't he tell us
that it was a fake note mold?

1809
01:59:21,250 --> 01:59:23,250
If he says that,
how will he be able to print it?

1810
01:59:23,833 --> 01:59:26,042
God! I hope he is still there.

1811
01:59:35,708 --> 01:59:38,417
Hey! Wasn't that Iron Abdullah's
driver driving the ambulance?

1812
01:59:38,583 --> 01:59:41,125
-Yes, Pappan!
-Jesus! Did Abdullah die?

1813
01:59:41,333 --> 01:59:44,208
No, Shajiyetta! What if he escaped in an
ambulance so that we can't catch him?

1814
01:59:44,333 --> 01:59:46,708
You're right!
Turn the van around, Pappan!

1815
01:59:46,833 --> 01:59:47,833
Get him!

1816
01:59:49,208 --> 01:59:51,875
-Turn it, Pappan!
-I won't spare you!

1817
01:59:53,542 --> 01:59:54,542
Idiots.

1818
01:59:54,875 --> 01:59:57,417
When I asked for a place to hide,
you took me on top of a lorry!

1819
01:59:58,042 --> 02:00:00,583
We're lucky that the driver felt
sorry for us and let us get down.

1820
02:00:00,667 --> 02:00:02,708
Or else we would've had to
get down at Coimbatore.

1821
02:00:02,875 --> 02:00:03,875
Donkeys!

1822
02:00:04,875 --> 02:00:06,208
Now, don't worry about anything!

1823
02:00:06,708 --> 02:00:10,708
If we see him, I'll just shoot him
to death like this...

1824
02:00:19,583 --> 02:00:20,875
I should be blaming myself!

1825
02:00:21,750 --> 02:00:24,250
If I bought three elephants
instead of feeding you guys...

1826
02:00:25,750 --> 02:00:28,250
I could have sent them to Thrisshur Pooram
and made some money!

1827
02:00:32,333 --> 02:00:34,625
-I have a doubt.
-Yes. Tell me. Ask me.

1828
02:00:34,750 --> 02:00:36,167
Doubts are always good.

1829
02:00:36,375 --> 02:00:37,833
-During the Thrisshur Pooram...
-Yes.

1830
02:00:37,958 --> 02:00:39,250
...if we display our three elephants

1831
02:00:39,375 --> 02:00:41,000
among all those elephants,
will they get sold?

1832
02:00:45,417 --> 02:00:48,958
Dude, the dynamite!
I haven't removed the pin! No!

1833
02:00:49,542 --> 02:00:51,417
I haven't removed the pin.
It won't explode.

1834
02:00:51,542 --> 02:00:54,167
No need to get scared.
I haven't removed the pin.

1835
02:01:04,167 --> 02:01:05,375
-Dude!
-Dude!

1836
02:01:05,458 --> 02:01:07,083
This is not how you make parottas.

1837
02:01:07,250 --> 02:01:09,625
-With egg and sugar--
-You should do it like this.

1838
02:01:09,708 --> 02:01:10,875
Dude, get up.

1839
02:01:10,958 --> 02:01:12,792
Dude, you're not the old parotta dude.

1840
02:01:12,875 --> 02:01:14,000
You're the Bangkok Dude.

1841
02:01:14,125 --> 02:01:16,292
An ambulance is coming. Stop it!

1842
02:01:16,417 --> 02:01:20,292
Get up, Dude! Stop! Stop, I say!

1843
02:01:21,083 --> 02:01:24,375
Lonappan, what's that noise there?
Why did you stop?

1844
02:01:24,458 --> 02:01:26,500
This ambulance is not for patients.

1845
02:01:26,625 --> 02:01:28,583
So you're only taking
aunties going to weddings?

1846
02:01:29,833 --> 02:01:32,583
Lonappan, who is this?
What is all this?

1847
02:01:33,333 --> 02:01:36,667
-Come here.
-Please take me also!

1848
02:01:37,458 --> 02:01:38,917
He's gone!

1849
02:01:49,583 --> 02:01:50,708
Who are you?

1850
02:01:51,208 --> 02:01:52,875
-What?
-No!

1851
02:01:53,583 --> 02:01:56,208
-No! What is that?
-I won't give it.

1852
02:01:56,333 --> 02:01:58,833
You won't give it?
What won't you give?

1853
02:02:06,083 --> 02:02:07,333
You...

1854
02:02:09,875 --> 02:02:12,083
Pappan, go fast!

1855
02:02:12,292 --> 02:02:14,458
This is not that mortgaged bullet.
It's a van.

1856
02:02:14,625 --> 02:02:17,000
Shajiyetta, those medicine guys
from Bengal are calling.

1857
02:02:17,125 --> 02:02:19,458
Ikka, hang up. Police will trace the call.

1858
02:02:21,000 --> 02:02:22,417
Pappan, it's them!

1859
02:02:24,292 --> 02:02:25,875
Oh, God!

1860
02:02:25,958 --> 02:02:28,333
-Get out!
-God! Save me!

1861
02:02:28,750 --> 02:02:31,458
-Save me!
-Shajiyetta, that's Abdullah!

1862
02:02:31,875 --> 02:02:33,000
Hey! Isn't that the gunman?

1863
02:02:37,000 --> 02:02:40,958
Oh, no! Bloody village dwellers!
Start! Close the door! Let's go!

1864
02:02:42,125 --> 02:02:43,167
Oh, God!

1865
02:02:46,000 --> 02:02:47,958
-Abu, let's get our stuff back.
-He didn't die?

1866
02:02:48,917 --> 02:02:51,458
That gunman gave you the kick
we should have given you!

1867
02:02:51,583 --> 02:02:54,792
What did you say?
You have a deep love for antiques, right?

1868
02:02:54,917 --> 02:02:56,792
Here's the money for your love!
Give us our stuff.

1869
02:02:56,875 --> 02:03:00,125
Everything is gone! He took everything
in that ambulance.

1870
02:03:00,625 --> 02:03:02,042
Ambulance? Abu, get in.

1871
02:03:02,500 --> 02:03:05,500
-Shaji, I'll also come. Let's go together.
-Throw this thing away, man!

1872
02:03:05,958 --> 02:03:07,750
-Are you avoiding me?
-Start the van!

1873
02:03:08,167 --> 02:03:10,167
Let's go! Let's go!

1874
02:03:11,750 --> 02:03:14,292
-Get lost, you scrap man!
-Chase!

1875
02:03:15,833 --> 02:03:17,917
Oh, God! My money mint is gone!

1876
02:03:19,208 --> 02:03:21,333
If not me, then no one needs to have it.
I'll sort you out now.

1877
02:03:22,458 --> 02:03:24,208
Looks like my cap will be short-lived.

1878
02:03:24,417 --> 02:03:26,750
And some idiots along with me.
What do I do?

1879
02:03:26,875 --> 02:03:28,042
My cap!

1880
02:03:34,583 --> 02:03:35,833
Why are you crying?

1881
02:03:36,333 --> 02:03:41,292
I'm crying because you will be in jail
before I can complete my studies!

1882
02:03:41,833 --> 02:03:45,125
Elephants have flown away in the storm,
and you're worried about your underwear?

1883
02:03:45,208 --> 02:03:47,417
-When did that happen?
-One tight slap!

1884
02:03:51,958 --> 02:03:54,292
True caller. Iron Abdullah.

1885
02:03:55,125 --> 02:03:56,458
Who is this nuisance?

1886
02:03:58,417 --> 02:04:00,375
-SI Shemeer.
-This is an anonymous call.

1887
02:04:00,708 --> 02:04:02,208
<i>I'm not interested in revealing my name.</i>

1888
02:04:02,500 --> 02:04:04,875
You needn't say your name.
Just tell me the matter.

1889
02:04:05,292 --> 02:04:07,208
That Shaji Pappan and boys

1890
02:04:07,583 --> 02:04:12,208
have gone up the Kulamavu dam
with that fake money mint.

1891
02:04:12,625 --> 02:04:14,042
<i>You can catch them</i>
<i>if you go now.</i>

1892
02:04:14,250 --> 02:04:16,667
-Govindan, start the car now!
-Okay, sir.

1893
02:04:21,500 --> 02:04:22,500
I won't spare you!

1894
02:04:23,167 --> 02:04:26,000
But how did this West Indian
beast get involved in all this?

1895
02:04:26,375 --> 02:04:28,917
When there are bad times,
all these scoundrels arrive!

1896
02:04:29,042 --> 02:04:30,125
Go fast, Pappan!

1897
02:04:30,750 --> 02:04:33,333
That's an ambulance. If I go faster,
all of us will have to travel in that!

1898
02:04:33,542 --> 02:04:35,083
Pappan, stop the van!

1899
02:04:35,542 --> 02:04:37,375
-What happened?
-I want to pee.

1900
02:04:38,542 --> 02:04:41,042
-I'll slice it off!
-My sweetheart!

1901
02:04:48,250 --> 02:04:49,833
Shajiyetta, hurry up!

1902
02:04:57,458 --> 02:05:00,250
Who blocked Pappan's van?
Get out and hit him, Pappan!

1903
02:05:04,833 --> 02:05:07,250
-Who's this one-eyed man?
-Oh, God! Uthup!

1904
02:05:07,458 --> 02:05:08,792
Will Uthup finish us, Pappan?

1905
02:05:09,250 --> 02:05:11,583
Shaji Pappan! Come out.

1906
02:05:11,875 --> 02:05:15,833
He must have understood
that we did it, right?

1907
02:05:16,458 --> 02:05:20,208
-If I don't come back, take my body home.
<i>-</i>Shall I order a wreath, Pappan?

1908
02:05:25,375 --> 02:05:29,333
What happened, Uthup Achaya?
Are you going to the church like pirates?

1909
02:05:32,125 --> 02:05:35,250
After that incident,
the opposition bashed me up royally.

1910
02:05:35,958 --> 02:05:37,958
So I was in the hospital for three weeks.

1911
02:05:38,500 --> 02:05:41,458
From there, the police took me
and put me in jail for a few days.

1912
02:05:41,875 --> 02:05:42,792
Not just that...

1913
02:05:43,542 --> 02:05:45,375
they burnt my wig too!

1914
02:05:47,833 --> 02:05:49,083
Oops! The window is closed.

1915
02:05:49,375 --> 02:05:50,917
You should tell Stella...

1916
02:05:51,750 --> 02:05:53,792
that the brake failed
because it was an old Jeep.

1917
02:05:54,167 --> 02:05:57,083
Look! I've bought a new car.
On the way from here,

1918
02:05:57,542 --> 02:05:59,250
I can brake anywhere I want with this car.

1919
02:05:59,708 --> 02:06:00,958
Really?

1920
02:06:01,958 --> 02:06:03,875
-What is this?
-Give this to Stella.

1921
02:06:04,708 --> 02:06:06,250
Uthup Achayan's Drum Stick!

1922
02:06:06,750 --> 02:06:07,958
Sheesh!

1923
02:06:09,083 --> 02:06:11,125
-I'll give it to her.
-All of you, get in.

1924
02:06:15,375 --> 02:06:18,833
-That loser is as old as Kerala.
-Pappan, come and get in fast.

1925
02:06:19,292 --> 02:06:21,583
-Let's go!
-He wants me to give it to Stella.

1926
02:06:21,708 --> 02:06:23,375
We'll use it as munchies.

1927
02:06:25,042 --> 02:06:26,167
Hurry up, Pappan!

1928
02:06:26,292 --> 02:06:28,333
Shut up!
This van even running is a big deal!

1929
02:06:32,958 --> 02:06:35,708
How are they able to follow us
wherever we go?

1930
02:06:35,792 --> 02:06:37,333
That's what I don't understand, Dude.

1931
02:06:39,833 --> 02:06:41,708
You idiot! Turn off the siren!

1932
02:06:42,667 --> 02:06:44,750
-Turn the siren off!
-That's true!

1933
02:06:44,958 --> 02:06:46,833
We could have escaped
from them ten kilometers back.

1934
02:06:47,333 --> 02:06:49,542
And now they're complaining
that we're being followed!

1935
02:07:12,500 --> 02:07:15,000
-What is this?
-The van crashed inside the tunnel, Dude.

1936
02:07:15,083 --> 02:07:15,958
What tunnel?

1937
02:07:16,083 --> 02:07:17,917
We don't know, Dude.
It's dark all around. Let's check.

1938
02:07:18,000 --> 02:07:20,042
-Open your eyes and look!
-Turn on the light!

1939
02:07:20,458 --> 02:07:21,958
Open it and look.

1940
02:07:23,042 --> 02:07:24,250
Did the tunnel swallow us?

1941
02:07:24,958 --> 02:07:27,125
-What is this?
-I don't want to go to my mother!

1942
02:07:27,417 --> 02:07:29,083
-Why?
-She's dead!

1943
02:07:29,250 --> 02:07:30,917
Well, that, and because we've
crashed in here.

1944
02:07:33,625 --> 02:07:34,625
Boss!

1945
02:07:39,500 --> 02:07:41,375
Dude, we are moving again!

1946
02:07:44,083 --> 02:07:46,708
-But we are not driving.
-Not us?

1947
02:07:47,750 --> 02:07:48,875
Then who is it?

1948
02:07:52,542 --> 02:07:55,125
How dare you mess with me?

1949
02:07:56,250 --> 02:07:59,625
Now you'll be making parottas
your entire life!

1950
02:08:12,083 --> 02:08:14,458
Go forward. Turn!

1951
02:08:15,167 --> 02:08:17,875
Stop near our men. Forward!

1952
02:08:22,417 --> 02:08:23,500
Get the ambulance out,

1953
02:08:23,625 --> 02:08:26,833
keep him alone inside, beat him
to pulp and bring him to our hotel!

1954
02:08:27,000 --> 02:08:30,292
Most importantly, you should beat him
and turn him into minced meat! Go!

1955
02:08:35,917 --> 02:08:39,000
You should've thought about that when
you threw away all those guns and bombs!

1956
02:08:39,958 --> 02:08:42,708
Brother, I'll only take that money mint!
Please.

1957
02:08:43,083 --> 02:08:45,958
Bro, please give it to me and me alone.
What is this, bro?

1958
02:08:46,083 --> 02:08:47,833
Do you need that mint
to make parottas?

1959
02:08:50,042 --> 02:08:51,250
Brother, please.

1960
02:08:51,333 --> 02:08:52,833
Brother! Brother!

1961
02:08:55,208 --> 02:08:58,375
-Again, those village dwellers!
-Shajiyetta, it's him!

1962
02:08:59,792 --> 02:09:01,042
Fools!

1963
02:09:10,833 --> 02:09:11,833
Pappan!

1964
02:09:12,417 --> 02:09:14,250
-Where?
-There!

1965
02:09:15,667 --> 02:09:17,167
There it is! Got it!

1966
02:09:18,417 --> 02:09:20,708
We've looked all over for you, my dear!

1967
02:09:22,083 --> 02:09:24,333
Please don't surrender me to those
intelligence officers, sir.

1968
02:09:24,875 --> 02:09:26,917
I don't even know Hindi.

1969
02:09:28,500 --> 02:09:30,458
I'll catch them, sir. Definitely!

1970
02:09:30,917 --> 02:09:32,792
Please give me one hour.

1971
02:09:36,000 --> 02:09:38,542
-What is it?
-Sir, it's that Satan Xavier.

1972
02:09:43,792 --> 02:09:44,792
Sir!

1973
02:09:45,208 --> 02:09:46,458
Isn't that Shemeer?

1974
02:09:46,958 --> 02:09:48,417
Sir, shall I give way?

1975
02:09:49,375 --> 02:09:50,625
Yes. Go ahead.

1976
02:09:51,042 --> 02:09:54,333
Xavier, sir, shall we give way to them?

1977
02:09:55,250 --> 02:09:58,083
-He will give way.
-Never give way to him.

1978
02:09:58,250 --> 02:10:01,208
He has been troubling the police
for a long time now.

1979
02:10:01,375 --> 02:10:03,833
Even last week, he scared us
with that bomb on a plate.

1980
02:10:03,958 --> 02:10:06,542
-True!
-What more do you have to lose, sir?

1981
02:10:06,792 --> 02:10:07,792
Get lost!

1982
02:10:08,000 --> 02:10:10,333
Govindan, blow that horn loud and clear!

1983
02:10:10,958 --> 02:10:13,333
-Govindan, come on!
-Okay, sir.

1984
02:10:13,917 --> 02:10:17,458
-Sir, they've blown the horn.
-Idiot, Shemeer.

1985
02:10:17,708 --> 02:10:19,375
He's making a psychological move.

1986
02:10:19,875 --> 02:10:21,292
Let him have the high beams from me.

1987
02:10:22,500 --> 02:10:24,167
Sir, they turned the light on!

1988
02:10:24,708 --> 02:10:26,292
-You also turn the light on.
-Done, sir.

1989
02:10:26,375 --> 02:10:29,083
That's it. We needed some color bulbs
as well, sir.

1990
02:10:29,250 --> 02:10:30,250
Correct.

1991
02:10:33,125 --> 02:10:35,417
Then this Xavier will put an end to this.

1992
02:10:35,583 --> 02:10:38,125
But, sir,
shall we give them a little way?

1993
02:10:38,417 --> 02:10:42,000
Xavier, sir, we don't have time for this.
Why should we wage wars now?

1994
02:10:42,250 --> 02:10:44,417
-I'm fed up!
-Keep quiet!

1995
02:10:44,667 --> 02:10:48,167
If I get scared of him once,
I'll have to be scared of him forever.

1996
02:10:48,667 --> 02:10:50,292
-Hold on tight!
-You also start the car!

1997
02:10:50,667 --> 02:10:52,708
I will teach you today
what psychology is all about!

1998
02:10:52,872 --> 02:10:54,875
He will lose this war and retreat
to the jungle with his Jeep!

1999
02:10:55,000 --> 02:10:57,792
-Start the car!
-Xavier, this is your end!

2000
02:10:58,208 --> 02:11:00,917
Until the last moment,
he will think that I'll move.

2001
02:11:01,208 --> 02:11:03,208
When he realizes that I won't,
he will move!

2002
02:11:03,375 --> 02:11:06,333
-Here you go, Shemeer. This is your end!
-Sir, shall we make way?

2003
02:11:06,417 --> 02:11:07,583
Shut up! Move forward!

2004
02:11:07,792 --> 02:11:09,667
-I need to put an end to this today.
-That's correct!

2005
02:11:09,792 --> 02:11:11,333
Shemeer, sir, you're super!

2006
02:11:12,292 --> 02:11:14,000
He didn't move!

2007
02:11:17,792 --> 02:11:19,833
Get lost!

2008
02:11:25,792 --> 02:11:27,458
He tried to mess with Pappan!

2009
02:11:27,792 --> 02:11:29,083
Pappan!

2010
02:11:29,167 --> 02:11:31,583
Pappan, shall we escape with this?
We can make millions!

2011
02:11:31,958 --> 02:11:33,250
Get lost, you scum!

2012
02:11:33,375 --> 02:11:35,250
I won't do such God-forbidden acts.

2013
02:11:35,375 --> 02:11:37,417
But, Shajiyetta, we can keep
it with us for three to four days,

2014
02:11:37,500 --> 02:11:39,875
print 30 to 40 million
and give it to the police gradually!

2015
02:11:39,958 --> 02:11:42,167
Yes. I'll give you a kick!

2016
02:11:42,375 --> 02:11:44,375
Didn't they call us insurgents already?

2017
02:11:44,583 --> 02:11:47,292
So you're all saying we make it true?

2018
02:11:47,417 --> 02:11:50,375
How can we become insurgents?
We are helping the country, right?

2019
02:11:50,458 --> 02:11:53,417
They just need to print half, right?
Won't we print the rest?

2020
02:11:53,583 --> 02:11:56,708
-That's correct!
-We should surrender this to the police.

2021
02:11:57,167 --> 02:12:00,208
Not so easily though.
Two birds with one stone!

2022
02:12:00,333 --> 02:12:02,542
Call Sarbath Shemeer.

2023
02:12:02,958 --> 02:12:04,250
Let me call that other scoundrel.

2024
02:12:04,417 --> 02:12:07,292
<i>Since the original mold was leaked...</i>

2025
02:12:07,375 --> 02:12:08,250
Bro!

2026
02:12:08,375 --> 02:12:10,458
<i>...it will be difficult to</i>
<i>identify these fake notes.</i>

2027
02:12:12,958 --> 02:12:15,375
-Tell me. It's Lassar.
-Lassar!

2028
02:12:15,792 --> 02:12:17,333
This is Pappan. Shaji Pappan.

2029
02:12:17,708 --> 02:12:19,667
You must have heard everything, right?

2030
02:12:21,458 --> 02:12:23,208
So we're coming there with the stuff.

2031
02:12:24,042 --> 02:12:27,583
Not just 20,
let's print three billion or more!

2032
02:12:28,333 --> 02:12:31,542
Okay. I have the rest of the set up here.
Come here.

2033
02:12:32,208 --> 02:12:33,917
Okay then. See you.

2034
02:12:35,375 --> 02:12:36,375
Scumbag!

2035
02:12:36,917 --> 02:12:39,000
He's waiting.
I hope he doesn't hurt my boys.

2036
02:12:39,417 --> 02:12:41,708
I didn't know that your Pappan
is such a big shot.

2037
02:12:42,292 --> 02:12:43,833
So we're all the same kind!

2038
02:12:44,583 --> 02:12:45,583
Right?

2039
02:12:46,250 --> 02:12:50,000
Hey! Once Pappan becomes
a great smuggler,

2040
02:12:50,167 --> 02:12:51,833
-will he forget us?
-No!

2041
02:12:58,542 --> 02:12:59,542
Awesome!

2042
02:13:01,333 --> 02:13:03,375
Boss, whatever we stuck together
is correct, right?

2043
02:13:03,667 --> 02:13:04,875
Get lost!

2044
02:13:05,125 --> 02:13:07,417
Note Marty has been doing
this job for a long time!

2045
02:13:07,542 --> 02:13:09,375
I am the Governor
of Kunmamkulam Reserve Bank.

2046
02:13:09,875 --> 02:13:11,667
There's not even a little difference

2047
02:13:11,750 --> 02:13:13,500
between my notes
and the Reserve bank's notes.

2048
02:13:13,583 --> 02:13:15,208
Shut your mouth and put
this into the printer.

2049
02:13:15,458 --> 02:13:16,458
Don't screw things up.

2050
02:13:17,875 --> 02:13:20,833
Shajiyetta, we didn't know that you
were such a big shot.

2051
02:13:20,917 --> 02:13:22,250
That's okay, man!

2052
02:13:22,708 --> 02:13:24,208
It must be poisoned.
Don't drink it.

2053
02:13:24,750 --> 02:13:27,083
-So, how are things?
-We're under a lot of pressure!

2054
02:13:27,292 --> 02:13:28,542
A goon's job is like that.

2055
02:13:28,667 --> 02:13:30,583
-Send my greetings to your mom.
-I will.

2056
02:13:30,708 --> 02:13:33,750
I don't have to say anything more, right?
Good job, Pappan!

2057
02:13:34,375 --> 02:13:36,333
This is the first time I've dealt
with a smuggler,

2058
02:13:36,417 --> 02:13:38,083
who the entire country is searching for.

2059
02:13:38,250 --> 02:13:40,708
We'll have a blast here in Kerala.

2060
02:13:40,792 --> 02:13:42,917
We all can do that.
But first, let's talk business.

2061
02:13:43,042 --> 02:13:46,583
Yes! First, let's sell these tires
and split the money in half.

2062
02:13:46,833 --> 02:13:47,958
Cleetus, I'll slap you!

2063
02:13:48,500 --> 02:13:50,042
What's happening there?
One minute, Lassaretta!

2064
02:13:50,167 --> 02:13:51,583
Get me those prints.

2065
02:13:52,250 --> 02:13:53,875
Give me an original 500 note.

2066
02:13:54,542 --> 02:13:55,417
Here.

2067
02:13:59,000 --> 02:14:00,292
Awesome, Lassaretta!

2068
02:14:00,542 --> 02:14:02,042
Even the Reserve Bank Governor
couldn't tell

2069
02:14:02,125 --> 02:14:03,750
which is original and which is duplicate!

2070
02:14:04,083 --> 02:14:06,208
We are millionaires, Lassaretta!

2071
02:14:12,292 --> 02:14:13,917
Shall we call Sarbath Shemeer now?

2072
02:14:17,583 --> 02:14:19,542
Is this the time to drink sharbat?

2073
02:14:20,750 --> 02:14:21,958
Bloody idiot!

2074
02:14:25,917 --> 02:14:27,625
Lassaretta, there's a small problem.

2075
02:14:28,667 --> 02:14:31,333
In the new notes we printed,
Gandhiji does not have spectacles!

2076
02:14:34,292 --> 02:14:35,875
Let's go back to our old position.

2077
02:14:43,000 --> 02:14:46,750
Shajiyetta, this is what happens
wherever we go for a deal!

2078
02:14:48,083 --> 02:14:49,500
He's getting up!

2079
02:14:53,083 --> 02:14:55,458
Sir, the notes were banned
at midnight, right?

2080
02:14:55,917 --> 02:14:59,958
So when he woke up from sleep,
to click the photo for new notes,

2081
02:15:00,083 --> 02:15:02,125
Bapuji might have forgotten
to wear his spectacles.

2082
02:15:03,625 --> 02:15:04,958
Lasu is taller.

2083
02:15:05,333 --> 02:15:06,875
Pappan lost. Sit down.

2084
02:15:07,000 --> 02:15:08,000
Cleetus!

2085
02:15:08,292 --> 02:15:11,500
Hi. You have a sword, huh?
Is it a costume drama?

2086
02:15:14,250 --> 02:15:17,792
You tried to fool Lassar?
Bloody swine!

2087
02:16:31,875 --> 02:16:33,042
Finish them, Shajiyetta!

2088
02:16:40,625 --> 02:16:42,333
Pappan, hit them!

2089
02:16:56,167 --> 02:16:59,750
<i>Even Haji Mastan would salute</i>
<i>The brave and mighty Shaji Pappan</i>

2090
02:16:59,875 --> 02:17:04,083
<i>Even an atom bomb would defuse</i>
<i>On its own at the sight of Shaji Pappan</i>

2091
02:17:08,333 --> 02:17:10,083
You shouldn't have!

2092
02:17:14,958 --> 02:17:20,125
<i>We built a raft with just</i>
<i>Our valor in hand</i>

2093
02:17:20,708 --> 02:17:26,417
<i>As friends join</i>
<i>Together to row forward</i>

2094
02:18:14,208 --> 02:18:17,292
If some blood had splashed on my face,
it wouldn't have disgusted me!

2095
02:19:02,542 --> 02:19:04,042
Shajiyetta!

2096
02:19:08,250 --> 02:19:11,375
<i>The chest broadens with pride</i>

2097
02:19:11,458 --> 02:19:13,958
<i>The iron fists are shining</i>

2098
02:19:14,042 --> 02:19:19,167
<i>There's fire in both the eyes</i>

2099
02:19:19,667 --> 02:19:22,458
<i>When fury is at its peak</i>
<i>It's a game of fire</i>

2100
02:19:22,667 --> 02:19:25,458
<i>Like an out of control weapon</i>

2101
02:19:25,583 --> 02:19:30,792
<i>Once angered</i>
<i>He's a mighty male elephant</i>

2102
02:19:50,917 --> 02:19:56,625
<i>Even the whole world will crumble</i>
<i>At their hands</i>

2103
02:19:56,792 --> 02:19:59,625
<i>To reach the sky as lightning</i>

2104
02:19:59,750 --> 02:20:02,083
<i>Their mighty hearts are finding</i>
<i>Fresh paths</i>

2105
02:20:02,208 --> 02:20:04,958
<i>Those who set the fireworks aflame</i>

2106
02:20:05,042 --> 02:20:07,750
<i>Can answer the scorching sun</i>
<i>On the streets</i>

2107
02:20:07,917 --> 02:20:13,500
<i>O' mighty warriors, who are swimming</i>
<i>Across the raging dark sea?</i>

2108
02:20:14,542 --> 02:20:16,292
If you touch me, I will tolerate it.

2109
02:20:17,250 --> 02:20:19,083
But if you touch my boys...

2110
02:20:20,583 --> 02:20:21,792
I won't tolerate that!

2111
02:20:24,458 --> 02:20:27,417
<i>They swing on a mad elephant's tusk</i>

2112
02:20:27,542 --> 02:20:30,583
<i>They are daredevils with many tricks</i>
<i>Up their sleeves</i>

2113
02:20:30,750 --> 02:20:37,708
<i>Who is there to fight them</i>
<i>And stop them from blazing forward?</i>

2114
02:20:40,833 --> 02:20:41,833
You!

2115
02:20:50,333 --> 02:20:51,333
Hey, Pappan!

2116
02:20:52,167 --> 02:20:54,667
Have you seen actual dynamite?

2117
02:20:55,667 --> 02:20:56,875
One that explodes?

2118
02:20:57,667 --> 02:20:59,917
I kept this aside for you!

2119
02:21:00,375 --> 02:21:02,500
To use it if the need arises!

2120
02:21:10,625 --> 02:21:11,833
Kill him, brother!

2121
02:21:14,292 --> 02:21:18,000
<i>When death is about to strike,</i>
<i>not knowing what to do,</i>

2122
02:21:18,292 --> 02:21:19,958
<i>we would stand still</i>
<i>with a sheepish scared face!</i>

2123
02:21:20,125 --> 02:21:22,875
<i>Like this. Pappan alone wasn't scared</i>

2124
02:21:23,125 --> 02:21:27,000
<i>He had seen a sight</i>
<i>which none of us had seen.</i>

2125
02:21:46,042 --> 02:21:48,292
-Mr. Shaji, congrats.
-So be it.

2126
02:21:57,333 --> 02:21:58,500
What did he say, Shajiyetta?

2127
02:21:58,833 --> 02:22:00,167
I didn't understand.
But don't show that.

2128
02:22:00,292 --> 02:22:01,875
Even though the design went wrong
by mistake.

2129
02:22:02,083 --> 02:22:05,542
Printing it and leaking the design
is a serious crime.

2130
02:22:05,708 --> 02:22:08,208
For helping us to nab
the absconding criminal and gang,

2131
02:22:08,458 --> 02:22:09,875
who printed the fake notes,

2132
02:22:10,000 --> 02:22:12,917
and for giving information
to the local police, we thank you.

2133
02:22:13,083 --> 02:22:15,333
-Who wants thanks?
-Not only with the police department.

2134
02:22:15,500 --> 02:22:17,917
-Again?
-But the whole nation is thankful to you.

2135
02:22:18,458 --> 02:22:22,000
Sir! I have a doubt. Do they also have
a part to play in this?

2136
02:22:22,250 --> 02:22:24,458
-When things went out of hand--
-Shut up, you idiot!

2137
02:22:24,792 --> 02:22:27,417
And the one who was supposed
to receive this in the High Range,

2138
02:22:27,542 --> 02:22:29,792
if that guy in Mangalore regains
his senses, we'll make him say it.

2139
02:22:29,917 --> 02:22:32,458
For catching such a big fake note
gang, won't we get any reward?

2140
02:22:32,583 --> 02:22:35,167
Can't you give ten percent
of those fake notes to us?

2141
02:22:35,750 --> 02:22:36,750
You want the whole thing?

2142
02:22:37,125 --> 02:22:38,250
-Yes.
-No need!

2143
02:22:38,542 --> 02:22:42,500
For you, who avoided the liability
of millions to the country's economy,

2144
02:22:42,708 --> 02:22:44,000
from the Government...

2145
02:22:44,083 --> 02:22:45,708
Where would we store
all that money?

2146
02:22:45,875 --> 02:22:49,875
-You'll get a reward of 10,001 rupees.
-Ten thousand and one damn rupees?

2147
02:22:50,083 --> 02:22:52,125
This is why no one returns the money mint.
Understood?

2148
02:22:55,375 --> 02:22:56,833
Isn't that a bit too much, sir?

2149
02:22:56,958 --> 02:22:59,875
It won't even be enough
for Pappan's medicine!

2150
02:23:00,042 --> 02:23:03,292
And you'll be getting an official
message about the reward.

2151
02:23:03,500 --> 02:23:06,125
So, Shaji, thank you and all the best!

2152
02:23:08,667 --> 02:23:10,417
Fool. Poor boy.

2153
02:23:10,542 --> 02:23:12,417
-Hey, Cleetus. Where are you going?
-Pappan!

2154
02:23:12,875 --> 02:23:15,583
If you guys ever plan
on taking a selfie,

2155
02:23:15,792 --> 02:23:17,625
you should ask prior
permission from the station!

2156
02:23:17,958 --> 02:23:19,292
Sir, our cup?

2157
02:23:19,750 --> 02:23:21,958
It's a seized item.
We got it from the crime-scene.

2158
02:23:22,167 --> 02:23:24,625
The case should be done.
It could take five, six years.

2159
02:23:24,792 --> 02:23:26,333
Sir, we got it with so much difficulty--

2160
02:23:26,458 --> 02:23:27,542
-Pappan!
-What is it?

2161
02:23:27,750 --> 02:23:30,000
Just because you helped
us catch that Lassar,

2162
02:23:30,125 --> 02:23:32,208
who fooled us saying
that he died in a bomb explosion,

2163
02:23:32,375 --> 02:23:35,167
I didn't lose my cap.
That's why I'm letting you go!

2164
02:23:35,292 --> 02:23:36,292
Or else...

2165
02:23:36,375 --> 02:23:39,792
Sir, shall we take all those
exploded guys to the hospital?

2166
02:23:39,875 --> 02:23:41,792
Yes. Get someone to scrape them up.
You, come with me.

2167
02:23:41,917 --> 02:23:44,417
-Will you give it?
-No! I won't!

2168
02:23:45,708 --> 02:23:46,875
These policemen are rascals, man!

2169
02:23:46,958 --> 02:23:48,250
This is why I didn't become
a police officer.

2170
02:23:48,375 --> 02:23:51,250
Shajiyetta, what about your mom
and our club?

2171
02:23:51,583 --> 02:23:53,250
Everything was in the air, right?

2172
02:23:53,833 --> 02:23:56,667
By the time we get the cup
in our hands after the case,

2173
02:23:56,792 --> 02:23:58,208
we'll lose the club, Shajiyetta!

2174
02:23:58,750 --> 02:24:02,250
Club, cup, everything is gone, man!

2175
02:24:05,500 --> 02:24:06,500
Who's that?

2176
02:24:06,750 --> 02:24:07,917
What now?

2177
02:24:08,583 --> 02:24:11,000
-Shajiyetta, this--
-Who are these new losers?

2178
02:24:11,167 --> 02:24:14,333
This is our Fakru. Fakru!

2179
02:24:14,542 --> 02:24:16,000
Who was at the station then?
Ikru?

2180
02:24:16,125 --> 02:24:17,792
Didn't I tell you then
that it wasn't Fakru?

2181
02:24:18,333 --> 02:24:20,833
Hey, brother!
Are they your Abu and Cleetus?

2182
02:24:20,958 --> 02:24:22,500
Yes. Come here!

2183
02:24:22,833 --> 02:24:24,583
Shajiyetta, come out.

2184
02:24:25,625 --> 02:24:27,833
Brother Fakru! Where were you?

2185
02:24:27,958 --> 02:24:30,792
-We mistook the others for you--
-We looked for you all over.

2186
02:24:30,917 --> 02:24:32,000
Catch this!

2187
02:24:32,167 --> 02:24:34,708
What the hell did you do? Some other
people came and gave something else--

2188
02:24:34,833 --> 02:24:36,500
Shajiyetta! Dollar!

2189
02:24:37,042 --> 02:24:38,458
-What?
-Dollars!

2190
02:24:39,458 --> 02:24:41,625
We want Indian money!

2191
02:24:41,792 --> 02:24:44,333
-We don't have any money!
-Pappan doesn't lie.

2192
02:24:44,583 --> 02:24:45,792
Remove your chain.

2193
02:24:45,875 --> 02:24:47,708
Give me the money or give me this chain.

2194
02:24:47,833 --> 02:24:49,625
-Hey! What are you doing?
-Let them take it.

2195
02:24:49,917 --> 02:24:51,458
-It's rolled gold.
-Is it?

2196
02:24:51,583 --> 02:24:53,917
Our work is done.
Let's go!

2197
02:24:54,083 --> 02:24:55,083
Go fast!

2198
02:24:56,250 --> 02:24:58,792
-You fool! It's fake!
-Shajiyetta!

2199
02:24:59,000 --> 02:25:00,792
-Dollars.
-Dollars, man!

2200
02:25:01,083 --> 02:25:02,750
What do we do with dollars?

2201
02:25:02,958 --> 02:25:05,000
Shouldn't we go to America
to exchange this?

2202
02:25:05,167 --> 02:25:06,083
Then what?

2203
02:25:06,208 --> 02:25:08,292
Because Pappan has a case,
he won't get a passport.

2204
02:25:08,583 --> 02:25:09,792
Can't we exchange it here?

2205
02:25:09,917 --> 02:25:11,625
If so, they would have
exchanged it, right?

2206
02:25:11,750 --> 02:25:12,750
That's true.

2207
02:25:13,125 --> 02:25:14,625
Dude, those guys...

2208
02:25:14,750 --> 02:25:17,667
You guys are such fools!

2209
02:25:24,292 --> 02:25:26,500
I have seen that jeep somewhere.

2210
02:25:29,750 --> 02:25:32,667
I didn't get married for so long
to find a girl like you.

2211
02:25:32,875 --> 02:25:35,250
-But we could have told him.
-Ask him to get lost.

2212
02:25:35,375 --> 02:25:37,750
We'll go straight to Kulu
and then to Manali.

2213
02:25:39,750 --> 02:25:40,667
Shajiyettan!

2214
02:25:40,792 --> 02:25:42,583
-What did you say that for?
-Get lost!

2215
02:25:44,958 --> 02:25:46,458
My yellow shirt.

2216
02:25:47,625 --> 02:25:50,417
My necklace, my mundu, my trousers.

2217
02:25:50,708 --> 02:25:53,333
Some unlucky guy's wife, right?

2218
02:25:53,542 --> 02:25:55,208
-Who is this, Etta?
-Shajiyettan!

2219
02:25:55,750 --> 02:25:59,000
-He was your driver?
-Yes. I was his driver!

2220
02:25:59,250 --> 02:26:00,250
You loser!

2221
02:26:00,375 --> 02:26:02,292
-Do you know who he is?
-Don't tell her, please.

2222
02:26:02,417 --> 02:26:05,750
When I had a back sprain, he eloped
with my wife. This scoundrel!

2223
02:26:06,292 --> 02:26:08,500
-Are you married, Ponnappan Chettan?
-No.

2224
02:26:09,000 --> 02:26:10,000
Come with me. He's crazy!

2225
02:26:10,208 --> 02:26:13,792
Hey! I don't need anything.
Return my trousers at least!

2226
02:26:13,958 --> 02:26:15,708
Return my trousers!

2227
02:26:14,958 --> 02:26:55,708
TamilRockers

